{"abstract":"Objectives: Arginine is a caries-preventive agent that modulates the microbial composition of dental biofilms and raises pH via bacterial ammonia production. The effect of arginine on biofilm pH has only been measured in bulk, and it is unknown how treatment affects microscale pH developments inside dental biofilms. Moreover, little is known about arginine's impact on the biofilm matrix. This study investigated the effects of arginine on biofilm pH, matrix architecture and microbial composition in a saliva-derived biofilm model. Methods: 72-h biofilms were grown with or without sucrose, and arginine was either supplemented during growth or provided as pulsed treatment. pH was measured in different locations at the biofilm base using confocal-microscopy-based pH ratiometry. Matrix carbohydrates and extracellular DNA (eDNA) were assessed via fluorescence-lectin-binding-analysis and eDNA mapping. Microbial composition was determined by 16S rRNA gene sequencing. Results: Arginine supplementation during growth considerably raised the biofilm pH, despite the presence of sucrose, and counteracted sucrose-induced shifts in microbial composition. Pulsed arginine treatment, in contrast, had little influence on microbial composition, but still a significant effect on biofilm pH. Importantly, arginine treatment increased the pH variance between different biofilm areas, suggesting that local factors in the biofilm microarchitecture modulate the treatment response. Lastly, arginine supplementation reduced the abundance of matrix carbohydrates, while increasing eDNA levels. Conclusions: Arginine impacts biofilm pH at the microscale and changes the microbial and matrix composition in a saliva-derived biofilm model. Clinical significance: Arginine exerts caries-preventive effects via multiple mechanisms, including modulations of biofilm pH and matrix microarchitecture.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Assar, Sahar","Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","Chokyu Del Rey, Yumi","Lund, Marie Braad","Raittio, Eero","Schramm, Andreas","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Schlafer, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816514"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Assar, Sahar"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Eastern Finland"],"keyword":["16S rRNA","Confocal microscopy","Dental caries","Extracellular matrix","Fluorescent Dyes","pH ratiometry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microscale analyses of the effect of arginine on oral biofilms","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdent.2025.105863","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816514","identifier":[{"id":"105007774118","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40449826","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b95e53b1-264f-4cc4-b0b1-77973b424b3b"],"keyword":["16S rRNA","Confocal microscopy","Dental caries","Extracellular matrix","Fluorescent dyes","pH ratiometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C25EFA1036C79C616E7235124ECDCA18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdent.2025.105863","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"university of eastern finland","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Eastern Finland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sahar","key":"assarpau","last":"Assar","locid":"a48d9a06-13d6-444a-b2d1-080b6179a64e","name":"Assar, Sahar","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-2013","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Frost","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3db74fb4-c382-451d-bd24-abea0bc2092c","name":"Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yumi Chokyu","key":"delreypau","last":"Del Rey","locid":"22d33fad-da2e-4a05-8e4a-d39df9284c88","name":"Chokyu Del Rey, Yumi","name_org":"Del Rey, Yumi Chokyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Braad","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"ccca6a51-5b47-45b6-969c-b0c5ea95100c","name":"Lund, Marie Braad","orcid":"0000-0003-1543-1009","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eero Juhani","key":"raittiopau","last":"Raittio","locid":"c08351bf-55fc-4082-9e6e-cd59c6a6b513","name":"Raittio, Eero","name_org":"Raittio, Eero Juhani","orcid":"0000-0002-9258-9355","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40449826"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jdent.2025.105863","issn":["03005712","1879176X"],"issn_org":["03005712"],"journal":"Journal of Dentistry","paperid":"105863","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Dentistry","volume":"160"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007774118"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b95e53b1-264f-4cc4-b0b1-77973b424b3b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Microscale analyses of the effect of arginine on oral biofilms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816514","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Extracellular DNA (eDNA) in bacterial biofilms can form non-canonical structures like Z-DNA and G-quadruplex (G4), which enhance biofilm resilience by providing protection against mammalian DNases. However, the conformation of eDNA in dental biofilms remains unexplored. Using fluorescence immunolabeling and confocal microscopy, we examined dental biofilms from healthy and caries-active subjects, revealing B-DNA, G4-, and Z-DNA structures surrounding clusters of bacteria, with some structures directly associated with the bacterial cell surface. We demonstrated that these non-canonical DNA structures were resistant to mammalian DNase I. Using a Streptococcus mutans biofilm model, we visualised fluorescently labelled eDNA during enzyme treatment and identified both an experimental nuclease and a DNase I-chloroquine combination capable of removing eDNA that was resistant to DNase I. These findings suggest that G4 and Z-DNA structures represent novel targets for improved enzyme formulations in controlling dental biofilms and potentially other biofilms containing these secondary DNA structures.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Evans, Dominique Catherine","Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","Minero, Gabriel Antonio Salvador","Palmén, Lorena G","Knap, Inge","Tiwari, Manish K","Schlafer, Sebastian","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-815860"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise","Tiwari, Manish K"],"keyword":["Biofilms growth development","DNA Bacterial chemistry","Deoxyribonuclease I metabolism","G Quadruplexes","Humans","Microscopy Confocal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dental biofilms contain dnase i resistant z dna and g quadruplexes but alternative dnase overcomes this resistance","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00694-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-815860","identifier":[{"id":"40389511","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005425399","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12089357","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-631c1b39-ff8e-4b31-a299-a547ab303254"],"keyword":["Biofilms/growth & development","DNA, Bacterial/chemistry","Dental Caries/microbiology","Deoxyribonuclease I/metabolism","G-Quadruplexes","Humans","Microscopy, Confocal","Streptococcus mutans/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-78A66B293A0D49BF6DC420A23D88BB44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00694-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novonesis A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominique C S","key":"evanspau","last":"Evans","locid":"acb7dcc9-ffb2-44f4-8fb3-d4425be5f731","name":"Evans, Dominique Catherine","name_org":"Evans, Dominique C S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde F","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3db74fb4-c382-451d-bd24-abea0bc2092c","name":"Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","name_org":"Kristensen, Mathilde F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gabriel Antonio S","key":"mineropau","last":"Minero","locid":"cc436bce-1546-4216-bb08-ae06ac0300d2","name":"Minero, Gabriel Antonio Salvador","name_org":"Minero, Gabriel Antonio S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena G","key":"palménpau","last":"Palmén","name":"Palmén, Lorena G","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge","key":"knappau","last":"Knap","name":"Knap, Inge","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manish K","key":"tiwaripau","last":"Tiwari","name":"Tiwari, Manish K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40389511"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41522-025-00694-x","issn":["20555008"],"issue":"1","journal":"npj Biofilms and Microbiomes","paperid":"80","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"npj Biofilms and Microbiomes","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005425399"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-631c1b39-ff8e-4b31-a299-a547ab303254"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dental biofilms contain DNase I-resistant Z-DNA and G-quadruplexes but alternative DNase overcomes this resistance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-815860","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Adult intensive care unit (ICU) patients receive many interventions, but few are supported by high-certainty evidence. Randomised clinical trials (RCTs) are essential for trustworthy comparisons of intervention effects, but conventional RCTs are costly, cumbersome, inflexible, and often turn out inconclusive. Adaptive platform trials may mitigate these issues and have higher probabilities of obtaining conclusive results faster and at lower costs per participant. METHODS: The Intensive Care Platform Trial (INCEPT) is an investigator-initiated, pragmatic, randomised, embedded, multifactorial, international, adaptive platform trial including adults acutely admitted to ICUs. INCEPT will assess comparable groups of interventions (primarily commonly used interventions with clinical uncertainty and practice variation) nested in domains. Interventions may be either open-label or masked. New domains will continuously be added to the platform. INCEPT assesses multiple core outcomes selected following substantial stakeholder involvement: mortality, days alive without life support/out of hospital/free of delirium, health-related quality of life, cognitive function, and safety outcomes. Each domain will use one of these core outcomes as the primary outcome. INCEPT primarily uses Bayesian statistical methods with neutral, minimally informative or sceptical priors, adjustment for important prognostic baseline variables, and calculation of absolute and relative differences in the intention-to-treat populations. Domains and intervention arms may be stopped for superiority/inferiority, practical equivalence, or futility according to pre-specified adaptation rules evaluated using statistical simulation or at pre-specified maximum sample sizes. Domains may use response-adaptive randomisation, meaning that more participants will be allocated to interventions with higher probabilities of being superior. CONCLUSIONS: INCEPT provides an efficient, pragmatic, and flexible platform for comparing the effects of many interventions used in adult ICU patients. The adaptive design enables the trial to use accumulating data to improve the treatment of future participants. INCEPT will provide high-certainty, conclusive evidence for many interventions, directly inform clinical practice, and thus improve patient-important outcomes.","author_count":36,"contributors":["Granholm, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander","Kaas-Hansen, Benjamin Skov","Jensen, Aksel Karl Georg","Munch, Marie Warrer","Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Andersen, Lars Wiuff","Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Larsen, Rikke Faebo","Thorsen-Meyer, Hans-Christian","Collet, Marie Oxenbøll","Meier, Nick Frørup","Estrup, Stine","Mathiesen, Ole","Maagaard, Mathias","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Strøm, Thomas","Christensen, Steffen","Bruun, Camilla Rahbek Lysholm","Keus, Frederik","Rossing, Peter","Granfeldt, Asger","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Itenov, Theis Skovsgaard","Cronhjort, Maria","Laake, Jon Henrik","Hästbacka, Johanna","Pfortmueller, Carmen Andrea","Siegemund, Martin","Sigurdsson, Martin Ingi","Andersen, Lars Peter Kloster","Placido, Davide","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S04-090.69-803696"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Granholm, Anders"],"country":["Finland","Iceland","Netherlands","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Danderyd Hospital","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","Stockholm South General Hospital","Tampere University","Tampere University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital of Basel","University Hospital of Bern","University Hospital of Tampere","University Medical Center Groningen","University of Groningen","University of Iceland"],"keyword":["Adult","Critical Care methods","Humans","Intensive Care Units","Intensive care","Randomised clinical trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Research Design","adaptive platform trial","trial protocol"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incept the intensive care platform trial design and protocol","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.70023","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["INCEPT is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and Sygeforsikringen \\u2018danmark\\u2019, with additional support from Grosserer Jakob Ehrenreich og Hustru Grete Ehrenreichs Fond, Dagmar Marshalls Fond, and Savv\\u00E6rksejer Jeppe Juhl og hustru Ovita Juhls Mindelegat. The INCEPT-Albumin domain is partially funded by Danmarks Frie Forskningsfond. None of the funders have had any influence on the planning of the platform trial, and none will have any influence on the design, conduct, analysis, or reporting of any domains assessed on the platform. None of the funders will have ownership of any trial data."],"id":"S04-090.69-803696","identifier":[{"id":"40084471","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105000407158","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11907384","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-5b8a4186-1792-4795-b30d-b527902a8206","au-71405ed2-21d6-4ea3-8927-450b365fde7d","ku-9c