,"name":"Møller, Rikke S.","name_org":"Møller, Rikke Steensbjerre","orcid":"0000-0002-9664-1448","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38996765"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105236","issn":["23523964"],"journal":"EBioMedicine","paperid":"105236","publisher":"Lancet Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"EBioMedicine","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197745491"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","danish hospital for rheumatic diseases"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-dbfdac1e-af8b-4ebb-9f7b-e05a4f42ebb9","sdu-57a47505-d554-4a1f-86c4-809e4c24d41b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Distinct neurodevelopmental and epileptic phenotypes associated with gain- and loss-of-function GABRB2 variants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-751929","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The major human pathogen Staphylococcus aureus forms biofilms comprising of a fibrin network that increases attachment to surfaces and shields bacteria from the immune system. It secretes two coagulases, Coagulase (Coa) and von Willebrand factor binding protein (vWbp), which hijack the host coagulation cascade and trigger the formation of this fibrin clot. However, it is unclear how Coa and vWbp contribute differently to the localisation and dynamics of clot assembly in growing biofilms. Here, we address this question using high-precision time-resolved confocal microscopy of fluorescent fibrin to establish the spatiotemporal dynamics of fibrin clot formation in functional biofilms. We also use fluorescent fusion proteins to visualise the locations of Coa and vWbp in biofilms using both confocal laser scanning and high resolution highly inclined and laminated optical sheet microscopy. We visualise and quantify the spatiotemporal dynamics of fibrin production during initiation of biofilms in plasma amended with fluorescently labelled fibrinogen. We find that human serum stimulates coagulase production, and that Coa and vWbp loosely associate to the bacterial cell surface. Coa localises to cell surfaces to produce a surface-attached fibrin pseudocapsule but can diffuse from cells to produce matrix-associated fibrin. vWbp produces matrix-associated fibrin in the absence of Coa, and furthermore accelerates pseudocapsule production when Coa is present. Finally, we observe that fibrin production varies across the biofilm. A sub-population of non-dividing cells does not produce any pseudocapsule but remains within the protective extended fibrin network, which could be important for the persistence of S. aureus biofilm infections as antibiotics are more effective against actively growing cells. Our findings indicate a more cooperative role between Coa and vWbp in building fibrin networks than previously thought, and a bet-hedging cell strategy where some cells produce biofilm matrix while others do not, but instead assume a dormant phenotype that could be associated with antibiotic tolerance.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Evans, Dominique Catherine","Khamas, Amanda Batoul","Payne-Dwyer, Alex","Wollman, Adam J.M.","Rasmussen, Kristian S.","Klitgaard, Janne K.","Kallipolitis, Birgitte","Leake, Mark C.","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-767316"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Leake, Mark C.","Meyer, Rikke L.","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of York","York University Toronto"],"keyword":["Biofilm","CLIP tag","Confocal microscopy","Extracellular matrix","HILO","Monomeric superfolder GFP","SNAP tag"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cooperation between coagulase and von willebrand factor binding protein in i staphylococcus aureus i fibrin pseudocapsule formation","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioflm.2024.100233","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-767316","identifier":[{"id":"85207764917","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39555140","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11564979","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-283e3cc0-5ca8-44cd-91b2-616370ab96a2","sdu-c52460b6-e5dd-452c-bc41-a64ab5b11d5e"],"keyword":["Biofilm","CLIP tag","Confocal microscopy","Extracellular matrix","HILO","Monomeric superfolder GFP","SNAP tag"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7F751C18805B35A39448D6DC0ACBA4CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioflm.2024.100233","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276533507/1-s2.0-S2590207524000583-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - iNano-School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"york university toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"York University Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Molecular Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominique C.S.","key":"evanspau","last":"Evans","locid":"acb7dcc9-ffb2-44f4-8fb3-d4425be5f731","name":"Evans, Dominique Catherine","name_org":"Evans, Dominique C.S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanda B.","key":"khamaspau","last":"Khamas","locid":"2543fe5d-ede4-44e0-8a06-17ad5ce8fc37","name":"Khamas, Amanda Batoul","name_org":"Khamas, Amanda B.","orcid":"0009-0005-3480-5194","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Alex","key":"paynedwyerpau","last":"Payne-Dwyer","name":"Payne-Dwyer, Alex","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam J.M.","key":"wollmanpau","last":"Wollman","name":"Wollman, Adam J.M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian S.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"21e58e9a-2974-4ad4-b03b-04b3ab5eec0e","name":"Severin Rasmussen, Kristian","name_org":"Rasmussen, Kristian S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne K.","key":"klitgaardpau","last":"Klitgaard","locid":"a0230a75-f632-4365-b9d1-0d17d2d01551","name":"Klitgaard, Janne Kudsk","name_org":"Klitgaard, Janne K.","orcid":"0000-0001-5255-2980","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"kallipolitispau","last":"Kallipolitis","locid":"642f37f4-0a2d-459b-8092-0f1b21bebb6d","name":"Kallipolitis, Birgitte H.","name_org":"Kallipolitis, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0003-1233-9776","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark C.","key":"leakepau","last":"Leake","name":"Leake, Mark C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39555140"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bioflm.2024.100233","issn":["25902075"],"journal":"Biofilm","paperid":"100233","publisher":"Elsevier BV","status":"p","title":"Biofilm","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207764917"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-283e3cc0-5ca8-44cd-91b2-616370ab96a2","sdu-c52460b6-e5dd-452c-bc41-a64ab5b11d5e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cooperation between coagulase and von willebrand factor binding protein in <i>Staphylococcus aureus </i>fibrin pseudocapsule formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767316","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Recommendations for duration of treatment with antipsychotics before considering a switch vary from 2 to 8 weeks, although several studies suggest a rapid onset of action. The objective of this review was to estimate time to onset of action and time to maximum antipsychotic effect of asenapine, olanzapine, quetiapine, and zotepine (pines). We searched bibliographic databases for randomized, placebo-controlled trials in adults with schizophrenia estimating the antipsychotic effect of pines over time. Thirty-five studies including 6331 patients diagnosed with chronic schizophrenia were included. We estimated the standardized mean differences (SMD) of changes in symptom score from baseline to follow-up between intervention and placebo groups across studies using meta-analysis techniques. The summarized effect across all included pines administered as immediate-release formulations showed a statistically significant effect at week 1 (SMD, -0.20 [CI95% -0.28, -0.13]), which increased until week 3 (SMD, -0.42 [CI95% -0.50, -0.34]), after which the effect leveled off (week 6: SMD, -0.53 [CI95% -0.62, -0.44]). The sensitivity analyses of the individual pines confirm this finding, although data sparsity increases variability and limits conclusiveness of these analyses.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Meyer, Rikke","Skov, Kenneth","Dhillon, Inderjeet Kaur","Olsson, Emilie","Graudal, Niels Albert","Baandrup, Lone","Jürgens, Gesche"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-670997"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"onset of action of selected second generation antipsychotics pines a systematic review and meta analyses","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines11010082","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-670997","identifier":[{"id":"85146720020","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9855925","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36672589","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d0faa846-e106-4fe1-9757-87a72d7a6507"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1DF3C428BF2ABB2DBFF6E1FCBD7817B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346256586/biomedicines_11_00082.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines11010082","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kenneth","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"ec70bc13-11a2-4e19-9103-be5bc2d5af32","name":"Skov, Kenneth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inderjeet Kaur","key":"dhillonpau","last":"Dhillon","name":"Dhillon, Inderjeet Kaur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emilie","key":"olssonpau","last":"Olsson","name":"Olsson, Emilie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Niels Albert","key":"graudalpau","last":"Graudal","name":"Graudal, Niels Albert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Lone","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"22fabc84-50be-4fd7-8579-afc07cd5fb9b","name":"Baandrup, Lone","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Gesche","key":"jürgenspau","last":"Jürgens","locid":"d17dd3dc-8ce8-46d7-8c8b-0f54963a92bc","name":"Jürgens, Gesche","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36672589"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biomedicines11010082","issn":["22279059"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biomedicines","paperid":"82","status":"p","title":"Biomedicines","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146720020"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d0faa846-e106-4fe1-9757-87a72d7a6507"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Onset of Action of Selected Second-Generation Antipsychotics (Pines)-A Systematic Review and Meta-Analyses","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-670997","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Biofilm matrix-degrading enzymes are a promising approach to caries control, as they target determinants of biofilm virulence without compromising the microbial balance of the oral cavity. This study aimed to test the effect of treatment with a multiple-enzyme combination on the prevention and removal of a highly acidogenic in vitro-grown biofilm model dominated by Streptococcus spp. Materials and methods: Biofilms were grown in 96-well plates under aerobic conditions at 37°C for 24 hours using pooled saliva as inoculum and brain-heart infusion broth supplied with 5% sucrose and sterile saliva as growth medium. The effect of treatment with a combination of mutanase, glucanase and DNase on biofilm prevention and removal was investigated. Treatment was performed either during (prevention) or after biofilm growth (removal) and the remaining biofilm was quantified by crystal violet staining. Additionally, the treatment effect on biofilm matrix compounds was analyzed using confocal microscopy. Extracellular DNA was stained with TOTO-1, microbial cells with SYTO41 and matrix polysaccharides were visualized by including fluorescently labeled dextran in the growth medium. Treatment effects were analyzed using unpaired t-tests (p<0.05 was considered statistically significant). Results: Enzyme treatment reduced mean biofilm formation with 94%±1% SD (p=0.0001) and 69%±2% SD (p<0.0001) when performed during and after growth, respectively. Extracellular polysaccharides were on average reduced by 28%±6% SD compared to control treatment (p=0.02), but the mean ratio between polysaccharides and microbial cells remained unchanged (0.70±0.37 SD vs. 0.77±0.22 SD; p=0.74). No significant reduction in the amount of eDNA (p=0.74) was observed. Conclusion: Multiple-enzyme treatment is a promising non-biocidal approach to biofilm control.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rikvold, Pernille","Møllebjerg, Andreas","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Schlafer, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700062"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-08","place":"Egmond Aan Zee, nl","start":"2023-07-05","title":"Poster session presented at the 70th Annual ORCA Congress","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiple enzyme treatment reduces biofilm formation in a highly acidogenic in vitro model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000534630","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700062","ids":["au-c34c0044-7b4c-4db3-936c-91169af99e84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-5-6-B3CC39BF76D0553C3F5F08C27477C6D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000534630","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille","key":"rikvoldpau","last":"Rikvold","locid":"d5ef43bc-479a-4d2b-916a-7028a4618e80","name":"Rikvold, Pernille","orcid":"0000-0002-2431-6937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"møllebjergpau","last":"Møllebjerg","locid":"4176d27b-9e84-42e2-9357-cd93796c3046","name":"Møllebjerg, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000534630","issn":["00086568","1421976X"],"issn_org":["00086568"],"issue":"2","journal":"Caries Research","pages":"333","paperid":"52","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Caries Research","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c34c0044-7b4c-4db3-936c-91169af99e84"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Multiple-enzyme treatment reduces biofilm formation in a highly acidogenic in vitro model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700062","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Biofouling is a ubiquitous problem in many industrial systems including reverse osmosis (RO) desalination units where the biofilm impedes the water flow. It is essential to develop novel cleaning methods that are non-damaging and environmentally friendly. The most promising cleaning agents are enzymes, which can selectively cleave the components that stabilize the biofilm. However, biofilm-degrading enzymes are often difficult to identify due to the unknown matrix composition and lack of effective screening methods. To overcome this, a flexible screening platform was developed to evaluate enzyme treatment on fouling removal directly on RO membranes. The developed platform was used to identify enzymes that could degrade biofilms on fouled RO membranes. The membrane biofilms were destabilized by a range of enzyme groups, most effectively by proteases, lipases, DNase, cellulolytic enzymes, and pectin-degrading enzymes. The most effective enzyme formulations could clean the membranes more effectively than conventional chemical cleaning agents, removing 45 % of the biofilm compared with 0 %–19 % for the chemicals (p ≤ 0.001), indicating that enzymes have the potential to replace or complement chemical cleaning. The screening platform thus proved a potent tool for systematically studying biofilms and could be applied to combat biofilms in many other applications.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Møllebjerg, Andreas","Zarebska, Agata","Nielsen, Henrik Bangsø","Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","Sørensen, Sebastian R.","Seredynska-Sobecka, Bozena","Villacorte, Loreen O.","Gori, Klaus","Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-151249"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Møllebjerg, Andreas"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Reverse osmosis","Screening","optical coherence tomography OCT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel high throughput screening platform identifies enzymes to tackle biofouling on reverse osmosis membranes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-151249","identifier":[{"id":"85148771574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-26230021-488e-45a3-9f57-5b1ca6953c99"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Biological Fouling","Enzyme Cleaning","Reverse Osmosis","Screening","optical coherence tomography (OCT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-241149A25A9187CC159D3D42EE69980C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/418459054/1-s2.0-S0011916423001170-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology - WATEC Aarhus University Centre for Water Technology, Ny Munkegade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"grundfos","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GFS","l3nl":"Grundfos","l3nn":"Grundfos","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Grundfos","namevar":["Grundfos A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GFS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"møllebjergpau","last":"Møllebjerg","locid":"4176d27b-9e84-42e2-9357-cd93796c3046","name":"Møllebjerg, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Agata","key":"zarebskapau","last":"Zarebska","name":"Zarebska, Agata","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bangsø","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik Bangsø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea Benedicte Skov","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian R.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Sebastian R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bozena","key":"seredynskasobeckapau","last":"Seredynska-Sobecka","name":"Seredynska-Sobecka, Bozena","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Loreen O.","key":"villacortepau","last":"Villacorte","name":"Villacorte, Loreen O.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"goripau","last":"Gori","name":"Gori, Klaus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena Gonzales","key":"palménpau","last":"Palmén","name":"Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.desal.2023.116485","issn":["00119164","18734464"],"issn_org":["00119164"],"journal":"Desalination","paperid":"116485","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Desalination","volume":"554"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148771574"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Grundfos","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-26230021-488e-45a3-9f57-5b1ca6953c99"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Novel high-throughput screening platform identifies enzymes to tackle biofouling on reverse osmosis membranes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-151249","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Dental biofilms are complex medical biofilms that cause caries, the most prevalent disease of humankind. They are typically collected using handcrafted intraoral devices with mounted carriers for biofilm growth. As the geometry of handcrafted devices is not standardized, the shear forces acting on the biofilms and the access to salivary nutrients differ between carriers. The resulting variability in biofilm growth renders the comparison of different treatment modalities difficult. The aim of the present work was to design and validate an additively manufactured intraoral device with a dental bar produced by direct metal laser sintering and vat photopolymerized inserts with standardized geometry for the mounting of biofilm carriers. Additive manufacturing reduced the production time and cost, guaranteed an accurate fit of the devices and facilitated the handling of carriers without disturbing the biofilm. Biofilm growth was robust, with increasing thickness over time and moderate inter- and intraindividual variation (coefficients of variance 0.48-0.87). The biofilms showed the typical architecture and composition of dental biofilms, as evidenced by confocal microscopy and 16S rRNA gene sequencing. Deeper inserts offering increased protection from shear tended to increase the biofilm thickness, whereas prolonged exposure to sucrose during growth increased the biofilm volume but not the thickness. Ratiometric pH imaging revealed considerable pH variation between participants and also inside single biofilms. Intraoral devices for biofilm collection constitute a new application for medical additive manufacturing and offer the best possible basis for studying the influence of different treatment modalities on biofilm growth, composition, and virulence. The Clinical Trial Registration number is: 1-10-72-193-20.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rikvold, Pernille","K. Johnsen, Karina","Leonhardt, Dirk","Møllebjerg, Andreas","Nielsen, Signe Maria","Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Schlafer, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183240"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Schlafer, Sebastian"],"keyword":["Additive manufacturing","Bacteria","Confocal microscopy","Dental biofilm","Extracellular pH","Fluorescence","Image","Plaque","Scanning microscopy","Sequences","VIVO","Vat photopolymerization","Vitality","pH ratiometry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a new device for in situ dental biofilm collection additively manufactured by direct metal laser sintering and vat photopolymerization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1089/3dp.2022.0009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-183240","identifier":[{"id":"85177088173","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10599433","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000796019000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"37886402","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5e85749a-17c0-4dda-b2df-18570ca5a7cb"],"keyword":["BACTERIA","EXTRACELLULAR PH","FLUORESCENCE","IMAGE","PLAQUE","SCANNING MICROSCOPY","SEQUENCES","VITALITY","VIVO","additive manufacturing","confocal microscopy","dental biofilm","in situ model","pH ratiometry","vat photopolymerization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-892C567218DCE1B598EDAAE9B566022F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/408410228/rikvold-et-al-2023-a-new-device-for-in-situ-dental-biofilm-collection-additively-manufactured-by-direct-metal-laser.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1089/3dp.2022.0009","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille Thestrup","key":"rikvoldpau","last":"Rikvold","locid":"d5ef43bc-479a-4d2b-916a-7028a4618e80","name":"Rikvold, Pernille","name_org":"Rikvold, Pernille Thestrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2431-6937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karina Kambourakis","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"e6eea993-e93e-40a1-91a9-00475b587f63","name":"K. Johnsen, Karina","name_org":"Johnsen, Karina Kambourakis","orcid":"0000-0002-9764-8481","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dirk","key":"leonhardtpau","last":"Leonhardt","locid":"40bbb7fb-b780-4eee-92cf-91b091331a80","name":"Leonhardt, Dirk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"mollebjergpau","last":"Mollebjerg","locid":"4176d27b-9e84-42e2-9357-cd93796c3046","name":"Møllebjerg, Andreas","name_org":"Mollebjerg, Andreas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Maria","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d1316f0c-0b76-4efe-8f69-89122076619c","name":"Nielsen, Signe Maria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea Benedicte Skov","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37886402"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1089/3dp.2022.0009","issn":["23297662","23297670"],"issn_org":["23297662"],"issue":"5","journal":"3D Printing and Additive Manufacturing","pages":"1036-1045","publisher":"Mary Ann Liebert Inc.","status":"p","title":"3D Printing and Additive Manufacturing","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177088173"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5e85749a-17c0-4dda-b2df-18570ca5a7cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A New Device for In Situ Dental Biofilm Collection Additively Manufactured by Direct Metal Laser Sintering and Vat Photopolymerization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183240","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Biochemical and biomechanical signals regulate stem cell function in the niche environments in vivo. Current in vitro culture of mouse embryonic stem cells (mESC) uses laminin (LN-511) to provide mimetic biochemical signaling (LN-521 for human systems) to maintain stemness. Alternative approaches propose topographical cues to provide biomechanical cues, however combined biochemical and topographic cues may better mimic the in vivo environment, but are largely unexplored for in vitro stem cell expansion. In this study, we directly compare in vitro signals from LN-511 and/or topographic cues to maintain stemness, using systematically-varied submicron pillar patterns or flat surfaces with or without preadsorbed LN-511. The adhesion of cells, colony formation, expression of the pluripotency marker,octamer-binding transcription factor 4 (Oct4), and transcriptome profiling were characterized. We observed that either biochemical or topographic signals could maintain stemness of mESCs in feeder-free conditions, indicated by high-level Oct4 and gene profiling by RNAseq. The combination of LN-511 with nanotopography reduced colony growth, while maintaining stemness markers, shifted the cellular phenotype indicating that the integration of biochemical and topographic signals is antagonistic. Overall, significantly faster (up to 2.5 times) colony growth was observed at nanotopographies without LN-511, suggesting for improved ESC expansion.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Ghorbani, Sadegh","Füchtbauer, Annette","Møllebjerg, Andreas","Martensen, Pia Møller","Hvidbjerg Laursen, Sara","Kraft, David Christian Evar","Kjems, Jørgen","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Rahimi, Karim","Foss, Morten","Füchtbauer, Ernst-Martin","Sutherland, Duncan S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-682323"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sutherland, Duncan S"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Biochemical cues","Embryonic Stem Cells","Nanotopography"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein ligand and nanotopography separately drive the phenotype of mouse embryonic stem cells","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biomaterials.2023.122244","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-682323","identifier":[{"id":"85165090857","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37459700","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-362a42dd-df10-4b40-8216-3a7699d88025"],"keyword":["Biochemical cues","Biomechanical signal","Embryonic stem cells","Nanotopography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8FBC665247AA2DAEB8370A0E6B06F2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/418457644/1-s2.0-S0142961223002521-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biomaterials.2023.122244","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sadegh","key"