{"abstract":"Treatment of Staphylococcus aureus biofilm infections using conventional antibiotic therapy is challenging as only doses that are sublethal to the biofilm can be administered safely to patients. A potential solution to this challenge is targeted drug delivery. In this study, we tailored an aptamer-targeted liposomal drug delivery system for accumulation and delivery of antibiotics locally in S. aureus biofilm. In our search for a suitable targeting ligand, we identified six DNA aptamers that bound to S. aureus cells in biofilms, and we demonstrated that one of these aptamers could facilitate accumulation of liposomes around S. aureus cells inside the biofilm. Aptamer-targeted liposomes encapsulating a combination of vancomycin and rifampicin were able to eradicate S. aureus biofilm upon 24 h of treatment in vitro. Our results point to that aptamer-targeted drug delivery of antibiotics is a potential new strategy for treatment of S. aureus biofilm infections.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Pernille Ommen","Hansen, Line","Hansen, Bente Kring","Vu-Quang, Hieu","Kjems, Jørgen","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-180169"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"keyword":["Anti Bacterial Agents therapeutic use","Biofilms","Drug Delivery Systems","Humans","Liposomes","Microbial Sensitivity Tests","Staphylococcal Infections drug therapy","Staphylococcus aureus genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aptamer targeted drug delivery for i staphylococcus aureus i biofilm","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2022.814340","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-180169","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9104115","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35573794","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85130103742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-592b8007-49cb-4a7d-bfe4-cd21bbe751d5"],"keyword":["Anti-Bacterial Agents/therapeutic use","Biofilms","Drug Delivery Systems","Humans","Liposomes","Microbial Sensitivity Tests","Staphylococcal Infections/drug therapy","Staphylococcus aureus/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8BC031E252601940B4B112CD1DDFF014"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2022.814340","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"andersenpernilleommenpau","last":"Ommen","locid":"58da0d0a-5fe3-4f73-a179-046c37fc0b70","name":"Andersen, Pernille Ommen","name_org":"Ommen, Pernille","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"hansenlinepau","last":"Hansen","locid":"729ea402-8050-4923-a2a1-2bfeb5a6fd63","name":"Hansen, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente K","key":"hansenbentekringpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3f32b0a5-11b4-4137-8a23-11362648542f","name":"Hansen, Bente Kring","name_org":"Hansen, Bente K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hieu","key":"vuquanghieupau","last":"Vu-Quang","locid":"db401c9a-70b3-4233-afcf-702859b17d38","name":"Vu-Quang, Hieu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemsjørgenpau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35573794"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcimb.2022.814340","issn":["22352988"],"journal":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","paperid":"814340","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","title_org":"Frontiers in cellular and infection microbiology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130103742"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-592b8007-49cb-4a7d-bfe4-cd21bbe751d5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Aptamer-Targeted Drug Delivery for <i>Staphylococcus aureus </i>Biofilm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-180169","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Many patients with developmental and epileptic encephalopathies present with variants in genes coding for GABAA receptors. These variants are presumed to cause loss-of-function receptors leading to reduced neuronal GABAergic activity. Yet, patients with GABAA receptor variants have diverse clinical phenotypes and many are refractory to treatment despite the availability of drugs that enhance GABAergic activity. Here we show that 44 pathogenic GABRB3 missense variants segregate into gain-of-function and loss-of-function groups and respective patients display distinct clinical phenotypes. The gain-of-function cohort (n = 27 patients) presented with a younger age of seizure onset, higher risk of severe intellectual disability, focal seizures at onset, hypotonia, and lower likelihood of seizure freedom in response to treatment. Febrile seizures at onset are exclusive to the loss-of-function cohort (n = 47 patients). Overall, patients with GABRB3 variants that increase GABAergic activity have more severe developmental and epileptic encephalopathies. This paradoxical finding challenges our current understanding of the GABAergic system in epilepsy and how patients should be treated.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Absalom, Nathan L.","Liao, Vivian W.Y.","Johannesen, Katrine M.","Gardella, Elena","Jacobs, Julia","Lesca, Gaetan","Gokce-Samar, Zeynep","Arzimanoglou, Alexis","Zeidler, Shimriet","Striano, Pasquale","Meyer, Pierre","Benkel-Herrenbrueck, Ira","Mero, Inger Lise","Rummel, Jutta","Chebib, Mary","Møller, Rikke S.","Ahring, Philip K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588244"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Ahring, Philip K."],"country":["Australia","Canada","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Giannina Gaslini Institute","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Oslo University Hospital","The University of Sydney","University Hospitals of Lyon","University Medical Center Freiburg","University of Calgary","University of Genoa","University of Lyon","Université de Montpellier – Université Paul Valéry – EPHE","Western Sydney University"],"keyword":["Epilepsy genetics","Gain of Function Mutation","Humans","Loss of Function Mutation","Phenotype","Receptors GABA A genetics","Seizures"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gain of function and loss of function gabrb000000000003 variants lead to distinct clinical phenotypes in patients with developmental and epileptic encephalopathies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29280-x","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank the affecomcted individuals and their families for participating in this study. The Australian National Health & Medical Research Council grants APP1185122 and APP1081733 (N.A., P.K.A., M.C.). The Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF19OC0058749 to R.S.M.) and The Lundbeck Foundation (R324-2019-1083 to R.S.M.)."],"id":"S01-000.00-588244","identifier":[{"id":"35383156","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8983652","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85127704108","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3488b8c9-3e6e-4893-87e6-eca5ea9f2c37"],"keyword":["Epilepsy/genetics","Gain of Function Mutation","Humans","Loss of Function Mutation","Phenotype","Receptors, GABA-A/genetics","Seizures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5916CB8FAC76A1BB72E3FD7BB68B4CF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearch