y of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Gain-of-function and loss-of-function GABRB3 variants lead to distinct clinical phenotypes in patients with developmental and epileptic encephalopathies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-588244","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Staphylococcus epidermidis is the most abundant commensal bacterium of human skin. Despite protecting us from foreign invaders, S. epidermidis itself exploits human vulnerability when given the opportunity. Such opportunities arise when patients are immunocompromised or when biomedical implants present an opportunity to colonize the surface and form biofilms. S. epidermidis is one of the most frequently isolated organisms from implanted devices and from bloodstream infections. However, S. epidermidis infections are often recalcitrant to antibiotics because of biofilm-associated antibiotic tolerance. Furthermore, the emergence and spread of nearly pan-resistant strains is a considerable health concern. Symptoms can be subclinical, making diagnosis challenging, and treatment with antibiotics is inefficient. For now, infection prevention remains the best strategy available.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Skovdal, Sandra Maria","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-147231"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anti Bacterial Agents pharmacology","Biofilms","Humans","Staphylococcal Infections diagnosis","Staphylococcus epidermidis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jmm profile staphylococcus epidermidis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001597","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-147231","identifier":[{"id":"85141004571","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36306163","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1f396264-a26a-4384-8132-f49b679245ea"],"keyword":["Anti-Bacterial Agents/pharmacology","Biofilms","Humans","Staphylococcal Infections/diagnosis","Staphylococcus epidermidis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-555FF3352612F83CC1614C15F3076840"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001597","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra Maria","key":"skovdalpau","last":"Skovdal","locid":"8e6b7c72-2732-402b-940c-ca02967599bd","name":"Skovdal, Sandra Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36306163"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/jmm.0.001597","issn":["00222615","14735644"],"issn_org":["00222615"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","paperid":"001597","publisher":"Microbiology Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141004571"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1f396264-a26a-4384-8132-f49b679245ea"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"JMM Profile : Staphylococcus epidermidis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-147231","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Colonization of textiles and subsequent metabolic degradation of sweat and sebum components by axillary skin bacteria cause the characteristic sweat malodor and discoloring of dirty clothes. Once inside the textile, the bacteria can form biofilms that are hard to remove by conventional washing. When the biofilm persists after washing, the textiles retain the sweat odor. To design biofilm removal and prevention strategies, the bacterial behavior needs to be understood in depth. Here, we aim to study the bacterial behavior in each of the four stages of the bacterial life cycle in textiles: Adhesion, growth, drying, and washing. To accomplish this, we designed a novel in vitro model to mimic physiological sweating in cotton and polyester textiles, in which many of the parameters that influence bacterial behavior could be controlled. Due to the higher hydrophobicity, polyester adhered more bacteria and absorbed more sebum, the bacteria's primary nutrient source. Bacteria were therefore also more active in polyester textiles. However, polyester did not bind water as well as cotton. The increased water content of cotton allowed some species to retain a higher activity after the textile had dried. However, none of the textiles retained enough water upon drying to prevent the bacteria from adhering irreversibly to the textile fibers. This work demonstrates that bacterial colonization of textiles depends partially on the hydrophobic and hygroscopic properties of the textile material, indicating that it might be possible to direct bacterial behavior in a more favorable direction by modifying these surface properties.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møllebjerg, Andreas","Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","Gori, Klaus","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-176171"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"keyword":["Biofilms","Hydrophobicity","Microbiology","Skin","Textile"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the bacterial life cycle in textiles is governed by fiber hydrophobicity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/Spectrum.01185-21","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-176171","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8515937","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85119204308","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34643452","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-52139771-0566-4cd9-b709-81d27c18bcf1"],"keyword":["Biofilms","Hydrophobicity","Microbiology","Skin","Textile"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-260ECB536DA057BDEF7C12D785495D49"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/Spectrum.01185-21","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"møllebjergpau","last":"Møllebjerg","locid":"4176d27b-9e84-42e2-9357-cd93796c3046","name":"Møllebjerg, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena Gonzales","key":"palménpau","last":"Palmén","name":"Palmén, Lorena Gonzales","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"goripau","last":"Gori","name":"Gori, Klaus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34643452"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/spectrum.01185-21","issn":["21650497"],"issue":"2","journal":"Microbiology Spectrum","paperid":"e01185-21","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Microbiology Spectrum","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119204308"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-52139771-0566-4cd9-b709-81d27c18bcf1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The bacterial life cycle in textiles is governed by fiber hydrophobicity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-176171","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Staphylococcus epidermidis is a common cause of implant-associated infections, and this is related to its ability to form biofilms. Strain-to-strain variability in biofilm formation is likely caused by genetic differences. Here, we present a draft genome of S. epidermidis AUH4567, which was isolated from a central venous catheter infection.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Meyer, Rikke Louise","Skovdal, Sandra Maria","Marshall, Ian P.G.","Schreiber, Lars","Nørskov-Lauritsen, Niels","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228882"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome sequence of staphylococcus epidermidis auh000000004567 a clinical isolate from an infected central venous catheter","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/MRA.01254-20","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228882","identifier":[{"id":"85103518406","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33766906","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7996465","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-ae825aed-81dc-40c9-81f9-f9aec62cc8a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E900BA5369E82D07D3623B286C548ED5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/285208627/MRA.01254_20.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/MRA.01254-20","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra M.","key":"skovdalpau","last":"Skovdal","locid":"8e6b7c72-2732-402b-940c-ca02967599bd","name":"Skovdal, Sandra Maria","name_org":"Skovdal, Sandra M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ian P.G.","key":"marshallpau","last":"Marshall","locid":"25504f0f-4132-4611-8697-0019cedc5d5d","name":"Marshall, Ian P.G.","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-4687","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"schreiberpau","last":"Schreiber","locid":"2460b94a-19ef-4377-9199-6da80017584e","name":"Schreiber, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"nørskovlauritsenpau","last":"Nørskov-Lauritsen","locid":"89068fb2-6301-49b0-be19-410589959dcd","name":"Nørskov-Lauritsen, Niels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33766906"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/mra.01254-20","issn":["2576098X"],"issue":"12","journal":"Microbiology Resource Announcements","paperid":"e01254-20","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Microbiology Resource Announcements","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103518406"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ae825aed-81dc-40c9-81f9-f9aec62cc8a1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Genome sequence of staphylococcus epidermidis AUH4567, a clinical isolate from an infected central venous catheter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228882","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Functional amyloids are highly organized protein/peptide structures that inter alia promote biofilm formation in different bacteria. One such example is provided by a family of 20-45 residue-long peptides called phenol-soluble modulins (PSMs) from Staphylococcus aureus. External components such as eukaryotic host proteins, which alter self-assembly of bacterial amyloids, can affect the biofilm matrix. Here, we studied the effect of the highly prevalent human plasma protein fibrinogen (Fg) on fibrillation of PSMs. Fg inhibits or suppresses fibrillation of most PSMs tested (PSMα1, PSMβ1, and PSMβ2) except for PSMα3, whose already rapid aggregation is accelerated even further by Fg but leads to amorphous β-rich aggregates rather than fibrils. Fg also induces PSMβ2 to form amorphous aggregates and diverts PSMα1 into off-pathway oligomers which consist of both Fg and PSMα1 and cannot seed fibrillation. Peptide arrays showed that Fg bound to the N-terminus of PSMα1, while it bound to the entire length of PSMα3 (except the C terminus) and to the C-termini of PSMβ1 and PSMβ2. The latter peptides are all positively charged, while Fg is negatively charged at physiological pH. The positive charges complement Fg's net negative charge of -7.6 at pH 7.4. Fg's ability to inhibit PSM fibrillation reveals a potential host-defense mechanism to prevent bacterial biofilm growth and infections in the human body.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Najarzadeh, Zahra","Nielsen, Janni","Farzadfard, Azad","Sereikaite, Vita","Strømgaard, Kristian","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Otzen, Daniel E"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013028"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human fibrinogen inhibits amyloid assembly of most phenol soluble modulins from i staphylococcus aureus i","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.1c02333","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013028","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8412925","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34497891","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114309001","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-05e1ac47-4311-4def-956c-58ba8d3b3f28","ku-7723ad54-7d0a-4834-a6ea-56c6829fcb37"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-01FD0201DEBA6AC9364F5A71B6CA6B3D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286492733/acsomega.1c02333.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.1c02333","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biopharmaceuticals"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zahra","key":"najarzadehpau","last":"Najarzadeh","locid":"e8173487-17a3-4b1b-a596-370c1317568c","name":"Najarzadeh, Zahra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janni","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8b802f3-e9d1-431f-9a1b-160e2d0254fb","name":"Nielsen, Janni","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Azad","key":"farzadfardpau","last":"Farzadfard","locid":"2a1befa8-f54b-4cc2-b58c-f854e5838d3e","name":"Farzadfard, Azad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vita","key":"sereikaitepau","last":"Sereikaite","locid":"e4b1934f-f94d-46ac-8e04-89830d4e7ac6","name":"Sereikaite, Vita","orcid":"0000-0001-7497-4965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristian","key":"strømgaardpau","last":"Strømgaard","locid":"78f1a438-9c1e-4795-bf55-b266b5d2cde4","name":"Strømgaard, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2206-4737","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel Erik","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","locid":"0ec06c22-1f74-4dd2-a894-af30b6565766","name":"Otzen, Daniel E","name_org":"Otzen, Daniel Erik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34497891"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsomega.1c02333","issn":["24701343"],"issue":"34","journal":"ACS Omega","pages":"21960-21970","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Omega","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114309001"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-05e1ac47-4311-4def-956c-58ba8d3b3f28","ku-7723ad54-7d0a-4834-a6ea-56c6829fcb37"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Human Fibrinogen Inhibits Amyloid Assembly of Most Phenol-Soluble Modulins from Staphylococcus aureus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013028","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Numerous beneficial microbes thrive in the oral cavity where they form biofilms on dental and mucosal surfaces to get access to nutrients, and to avoid being carried away with the saliva. However, biofilm formation is also a virulence factor as it also protects pathogenic bacteria, providing them with an environment for proliferation causing oral infections. Oral hygiene relies on mechanical removal of biofilms. Some oral care products also contain antimicrobials, but effective eradication of biofilms with antimicrobials requires both a high concentration and long exposure time. In the present communication, we investigate the potential of using miniaturized drug delivery devices, known as microcontainers (MCs), to deliver the antimicrobial peptide, nisin to an oral multi-species biofilm. MCs are loaded with nisin and X-ray micro-computed tomography reveals a full release of nisin through a chitosan lid within 15 min. Chitosan-coated MCs display substantial bioadhesion to the buccal mucosa compared to non-coated MCs (68.6 ± 14.3% vs 33.8 ± 5.2%). Confocal monitoring of multi-species biofilms reveals antibacterial effects of nisin-loaded chitosan-coated MCs with a faster onset (after 3 h) compared to solution-based delivery (after 9 h). Our study shows the potential of using MCs for treatment of multi-species oral biofilms and is encouraging for further design of drug delivery devices to treat oral diseases.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Birk, Stine Egebro","Mosgaard, Mette Dalskov","Kjeldsen, Rolf Bech","Boisen, Anja","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Nielsen, Line Hagner"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-027093"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Birk, Stine Egebro"],"keyword":["Antimicrobial peptides","Bioadhesion","CT","Chitosan","Microcontainers","Multi species biofilm","Oromucosal drug delivery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"management of oral biofilms by nisin delivery in adhesive microdevices","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpb.2021.07.007","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF122), Denmark and Villum Fonden (Grant No. 9301), Denmark for Intelligent Drug Delivery and Sensing Using Microcontainers and Nanomechanics (IDUN). Postdoc Signe Maria Nielsen, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center (iNANO), Aarhus University is thanked for her support in preparing the saliva-derived biofilm protocol. We thank Karina Kambourakis Johnsen, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health at Aarhus University for providing the saliva inoculum for the biofilms. Additionally, the 3D Imaging Center at the Technical University of Denmark is acknowledge. Graphical abstract was created with figures adapted from Servier Medical Art by Servier and licensed under a CreativeCommons Attribution 3.0. This work was supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF122), Denmark and Villum Fonden (Grant No. 9301), Denmark for Intelligent Drug Delivery and Sensing Using Microcontainers and Nanomechanics (IDUN). Postdoc Signe Maria Nielsen, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center (iNANO), Aarhus University is thanked for her support in preparing the saliva-derived biofilm protocol. We thank Karina Kambourakis Johnsen, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health at Aarhus University for providing the saliva inoculum for the biofilms. Additionally, the 3D Imaging Center at the Technical University of Denmark is acknowledge. Graphical abstract was created with figures adapted from Servier Medical Art by Servier and licensed under a CreativeCommons Attribution 3.0."],"id":"S02-100.00-027093","identifier":[{"id":"34302949","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111490668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c6ff27ff-396a-4ac4-abde-f71e0d70880f","dtu-f4cc1ae5-6a99-4c4f-92b1-c889048ccee6"],"keyword":["Antimicrobial peptides","Bioadhesion","Chitosan","Microcontainers","Multi-species biofilm","Oromucosal drug delivery","µCT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FF459D7B4D42C7A7AF97CECE4F9A8047"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/264654245/1_s2.0_S0939641121001880_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpb.2021.07.007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/285202377/1_s2.0_S0939641121001880_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Center for Intelligent Drug Delivery and Sensing Using Microcontainers and Nanomechanics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Drug Delivery and Sensing, Nanoprobes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Egebro","key":"birkpau","last":"Birk","locid":"017cf9e2-5f01-451d-b6db-d75abc7dbd79","name":"Birk, Stine Egebro","orcid":"0000-0001-9902-9177","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Dalskov","key":"mosgaardpau","last":"Mosgaard","locid":"8a6d5603-663c-4bea-be07-326a3715625a","name":"Mosgaard, Mette Dalskov","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rolf Bech","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"76955b71-90e9-40f0-8093-ed56053c96c4","name":"Kjeldsen, Rolf Bech","orcid":"0000-0001-7475-8939","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Hagner","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a9a7a51b-9e8f-40cc-b691-6e64d62e7765","name":"Nielsen, Line Hagner","orcid":"0000-0002-3789-4816","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34302949"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejpb.2021.07.007","issn":["09396411","18733441"],"issn_org":["09396411"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmaceutics and Biopharmaceutics","pages":"83-88","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmaceutics and Biopharmaceutics","volume":"167"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111490668"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c6ff27ff-396a-4ac4-abde-f71e0d70880f","dtu-f4cc1ae5-6a99-4c4f-92b1-c889048ccee6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Management of oral biofilms by nisin delivery in adhesive microdevices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-027093","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective:Women experience an unhealthy change in metabolic risk profile at menopause. The purpose of the present study was to determine effects of resistance training with or without transdermal estrogen therapy (ET) on adipose tissue mass and metabolic risk profile in early postmenopausal women.Methods:A double-blinded randomized controlled trial, where healthy, untrained postmenopausal women were allocated to supervised resistance training with placebo (PLC, n = 16) or transdermal ET (n = 15) for 12 weeks. Endpoints with prespecified hypotheses were the change in total fat mass (FM) (main endpoint) and the change in visceral FM (secondary endpoint) from before to after the intervention. Additionally, prespecified endpoints of body composition, metabolic health-related blood markers, fat%, fat cell size, and lipogenic markers in subcutaneous adipose tissue (SAT) from abdominal and femoral region were explored.Results:Compared with the ET group, the PLC group experienced a greater reduction (time × treatment interaction P < 0.05) in total FM (PLC vs ET: -5.6% vs -1.1%) and visceral FM (-18.6% vs -6.8%), and femoral SAT (-5.6% vs 1.0%), but not abdominal SAT mass (-8.5% vs -2.8%, P = 0.15).The ET group improved their metabolic blood profile by reduced low-density lipoprotein, glucose and hemoglobin A1c compared with PLC (time × treatment interaction P < 0.05). The intervention induced changes in lipolytic markers of abdominal SAT, whereas no changes were detected in femoral SAT.Conclusion:Use of transdermal ET reduced adipose tissue loss, but improved metabolic blood markers when combined with 12 weeks of progressive resistance training in early postmenopausal women.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Dam, Tine Vrist","Jensen, Line","Thomsen, Christian Bejlegaard","Hjortebjerg, Rikke","Ringgaard, Steffen","Johansen, Frank Ted","Bengtsen, Mads Bisgaard","Mose, Maike","Lauritsen, Katrine Meyer","Søndergaard, Esben","Gravholt, Claus Højbjerg","Hansen, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-132960"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Mette"],"keyword":["Adipose tissue","Estrogen","Menopause","Metabolism","Resistance Training"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estrogen modulates metabolic risk profile after resistance training in early postmenopausal women a randomized controlled trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85121474144","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-132960","identifier":[{"id":"85121474144","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34726661","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-065d9a9c-3174-4cd4-8655-4b1fb5be820b"],"keyword":["Adipose tissue","Estrogen","Menopause","Metabolism","Resistance training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CF35E3A1F7AB21F79DDD19102399CC5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Sport Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Vrist","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"80f50a8f-5217-4fdc-bfcd-b0f3ca5e4013","name":"Dam, Tine Vrist","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Barner","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"e136f41f-f605-4357-a0fb-258e8f7a10fc","name":"Jensen, Line","name_org":"Dalgaard, Line Barner","orcid":"0000-0001-7676-5323","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Bejlegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Christian Bejlegaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","locid":"d7f05783-92a6-4c22-9d46-9bd0128122b4","name":"Hjortebjerg, Rikke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen","key":"ringgaardpau","last":"Ringgaard","locid":"56699a63-018d-4902-b5f7-9816f8b7e4fc","name":"Ringgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0001-5353-7379","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank Ted","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"9760b379-ee35-4b6e-9b79-d508a982ea39","name":"Johansen, Frank Ted","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Bisgaard","key":"bengtsenpau","last":"Bengtsen","locid":"17a0209b-028a-40c1-8a5a-b65443ed3e56","name":"Bengtsen, Mads Bisgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8985-8385","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maike","key":"mosepau","last":"Mose","locid":"f083dcfd-61ef-4f1d-885a-f858c035ffae","name":"Mose, Maike","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meyer","key":"lauritsenpau","last":"Lauritsen","locid":"f4285b6b-d77f-4bfe-83f7-7b695160699f","name":"Lauritsen, Katrine Meyer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"35f76081-43f3-42ce-94b2-e60a44e59d5a","name":"Søndergaard, Esben","orcid":"0000-0001-8041-6994","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus H","key":"gravholtpau","last":"Gravholt","locid":"22ab3957-d834-426e-8ba5-3d45496b0d2a","name":"Gravholt, Claus Højbjerg","name_org":"Gravholt, Claus H","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"35b198ca-caef-48de-8570-21c9fbab1f8f","name":"Hansen, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-9383-8202","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34726661"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/gme.0000000000001841","issn":["10723714","15300374"],"issn_org":["10723714"],"issue":"11","journal":"Menopause","pages":"1214-1224","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Menopause","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121474144"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-065d9a9c-3174-4cd4-8655-4b1fb5be820b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Estrogen modulates metabolic risk profile after resistance training in early postmenopausal women : a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-132960","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction. Staphylococcus epidermidis is predominant in implant-associated infections due to its capability to form biofilms. It can deploy several strategies for biofilm development using either polysaccharide intercellular adhesin (PIA), extracellular DNA (eDNA) and/or proteins, such as the extracellular matrix-binding protein (Embp). Hypothesis/Gap Statement. We hypothesize that the dichotomic regulation of S. epidermidis adhesins is linked to whether it is inside a host or not, and that in vitro biofilm investigations in laboratory media may not reflect actual biofilms in vivo. Aim. We address the importance of PIA and Embp in biofilm grown in 'humanized' media to understand if these components play different roles in biofilm formation under conditions where bacteria can incorporate host proteins in the biofilm matrix. Methodology. S. epidermidis 1585 WT (deficient in icaADBC), and derivative strains that either lack embp, express embp from an inducible promotor, or express icaADBC from a plasmid, were cultivated in standard laboratory media, or in media with human plasma or serum. The amount, structure, elasticity and antimicrobial penetration of biofilms was quantified to describe structural differences caused by the different matrix components and growth conditions. Finally, we quantified the initiation of biofilms as suspended aggregates in response to host factors to determine how quickly the cells aggregate in response to the host environment and reach a size that protects them from phagocytosis. Results. S. epidermidis 1585 required polysaccharides to form biofilm in laboratory media. However, these observations were not representative of the biofilm phenotype in the presence of human plasma. If human plasma were present, polysaccharides and Embp were redundant for biofilm formation. Biofilms formed in human plasma were loosely attached and existed mostly as suspended aggregates. Aggregation occurred after 2 h of exposing cells to plasma or serum. Despite stark differences in the amount and composition of biofilms formed by polysaccharide-producing and Embp-producing strains in different media, there were no differences in vancomycin penetration or susceptibility. Conclusion. We suggest that the assumed importance of polysaccharides for biofilm formation is an artefact from studying biofilms in laboratory media void of human matrix components. The cell-cell aggregation of S. epidermidis can be activated by host factors without relying on either of the major adhesins, PIA and Embp, indicating a need to revisit the basic question of how S. epidermidis deploys self-produced and host-derived matrix components to form antibiotic-tolerant biofilms in vivo.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Skovdal, Sandra Maria","Hansen, Liva Kjær","Ivarsen, Diana Malskær","Zeng, Guanghong","Büttner, Henning","Rohde, Holger","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238152"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Hamburg"],"keyword":["Aggregation","Bacterial Adhesion","Bacterial Proteins metabolism","Biofilm","Biofilms growth development","Gene Expression Regulation Bacterial","Host components","Humans","Staphylococcal Infections microbiology","Staphylococcus epidermidis","extracellular matrix binding protein Embp"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"host factors abolish the need for polysaccharides and extracellular matrix binding protein in i staphylococcus epidermidis i biofilm formation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001287","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-238152","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8346721","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000638093200007","type":"wos"},{"id":"85103683495","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33492206","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-bea19448-194f-4abd-86fe-cd3f63f28c23"],"keyword":["Adhesins, Bacterial/metabolism","Aggregation","Bacterial Adhesion","Bacterial Proteins/metabolism","Biofilm","Biofilms/growth & development","Extracellular matrix-binding protein (Embp)","Gene Expression Regulation, Bacterial","Host components","Humans","PIA","Polysaccharides, Bacterial/metabolism","Staphylococcal Infections/microbiology","Staphylococcus epidermidis","Staphylococcus epidermidis/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A7A6E03A56FEE87645BD8C479C34481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8346721/pdf/jmm-70-287.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1099/jmm.0.001287","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afdeling, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hamburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra Maria","key":"skovdalpau","last":"Skovdal","locid":"8e6b7c72-2732-402b-940c-ca02967599bd","name":"Skovdal, Sandra Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liva Kjær","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"653924b2-77cf-4c6c-b9d3-9f1bd34da92f","name":"Hansen, Liva Kjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diana Malskær","key":"ivarsenpau","last":"Ivarsen","locid":"4d466e36-20f4-4cae-ac0f-c7c3fefca5ee","name":"Ivarsen, Diana Malskær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghong","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","locid":"41d64164-8293-4f51-b1b8-96ac2ccc6db5","name":"Zeng, Guanghong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henning","key":"büttnerpau","last":"Büttner","name":"Büttner, Henning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","name":"Rohde, Holger","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33492206"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/jmm.0.001287","issn":["00222615","14735644"],"issn_org":["00222615"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","paperid":"001287","publisher":"Microbiology Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Microbiology","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103683495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bea19448-194f-4abd-86fe-cd3f63f28c23"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Host factors abolish the need for polysaccharides and extracellular matrix-binding protein in <i>Staphylococcus epidermidis </i>biofilm formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-238152","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Listeria monocytogenes is a foodborne pathogen which can survive in harsh environmental conditions. It responds to external stimuli through an array of two-component systems (TCS) that sense external cues. Several TCS, including LisRK, have been linked to Listeria’s ability to grow at slightly elevated antibiotic levels. The aim of this study was to determine if the TCS LisRK is also involved in acquiring the high antibiotic tolerance that is characteristic of persister cells. LisRK activates a response that leads to remodeling of the cell envelope, and we therefore hypothesized that activation of LisRK could also increase in the cells’ adhesiveness and initiate the first step in biofilm formation. We used a ΔlisR mutant to study antibiotic tolerance in the presence and absence of LisRK, and a GFP reporter strain to visualize the activation of LisRK in L. monocytogenes LO28 at a single-cell level. LisRK was activated in most cells in stationary phase cultures. Antimicrobial susceptibility tests showed that LisRK was required for the generation of ampicillin tolerance under these conditions. The wildtype strain tolerated exposure to ampicillin at 1,000 × inhibitory levels for 24 h, and the fraction of surviving cells was 20,000-fold higher in the wildtype strain compared to the ΔlisR mutant. The same protection was not offered to other antibiotics (vancomycin, gentamicin, tetracycline), and the mechanism for antibiotic tolerance is thus highly specific. Furthermore, quantification of bacterial attachment rates and attachment force also revealed that the absence of a functional LisRK rendered the cells less adhesive. Hence, LisRK TCS promotes multiple protective mechanisms simultaneously.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Aslan, Hüsnü","Petersen, Maiken Engelbrecht","De Berardinis, Alberto","Zacho Brunhede, Maja","Khan, Nasar","Vergara, Alberto","Kallipolitis, Birgitte","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024156"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Aslan, Hüsnü","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Teramo"],"keyword":["Adhesion","Antibiotic tolerance","Listeria monocytogenes","Nanomechanics","Two component systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"activation of the two component system lisrk promotes cell adhesion and high ampicillin tolerance in listeria i monocytogenes i","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2021.618174","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024156","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7873292","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33584621","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85100974397","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9d688fce-9187-4795-aaf0-472f2a2c53be","sdu-e5c9e76f-0441-4180-acb9-380bfaa8c665"],"keyword":["LisRK","adhesion","antibiotic tolerance","listeria monocytogenes","nanomechanics","persister","tcs","two-component systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-20500D475F8CE7ED377E7C2930E2BBDE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/179899158/fmicb_12_618174.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2021.618174","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of teramo","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Teramo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hüsnü","key":"aslanpau","last":"Aslan","locid":"05e8885e-db36-4f96-8ecf-5263c578def8","name":"Aslan, Hüsnü","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken Engelbrecht","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"99c8dbe5-12c1-4b7b-bc1d-a2985885e525","name":"Petersen, Maiken Engelbrecht","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"deberardinispau","last":"De Berardinis","name":"De Berardinis, Alberto","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"zachobrunhedepau","last":"Zacho Brunhede","locid":"30ecb998-2e97-48c9-ac9b-82aacd776d9a","name":"Zacho Brunhede, Maja","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nasar","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"33b169a1-1e78-4233-849a-f3b8284d8331","name":"Khan, Nasar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"vergarapau","last":"Vergara","name":"Vergara, Alberto","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte","key":"kallipolitispau","last":"Kallipolitis","locid":"642f37f4-0a2d-459b-8092-0f1b21bebb6d","name":"Kallipolitis, Birgitte H.","name_org":"Kallipolitis, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0003-1233-9776","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33584621"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2021.618174","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"618174","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100974397"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9d688fce-9187-4795-aaf0-472f2a2c53be","sdu-e5c9e76f-0441-4180-acb9-380bfaa8c665"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Activation of the Two-Component System LisRK Promotes Cell Adhesion and High Ampicillin Tolerance in Listeria<i> monocytogenes</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024156","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background Medical implants are prone to bacterial attachment and development of biofilms. Biofilms cause the bacteria’s recalcitrance to antibiotics, resulting in a chronic infection that can be fatal. Previously, we have shown that the combination of antibiotics with fibrinolytic drugs such as streptokinase and tissue plasminogen activator (tPA) can eradicate methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) biofilms in vitro. In this study, we aim to compare the efficacy of antibiotic therapy with and without tPA to treat MRSA biofilms in a novel rat model of prosthetic vascular graft infections (PVGI) Methods Rats received a pre-inoculated vascular graft implanted in a. carotis communis. Implants were inoculated with approx. 4.4 CFU/graft of MRSA USA300 FPR3757. 10 days following surgery rats were randomized to either 1) vancomycin (50 mg/kg); 2) vancomycin + rifampicin (25 mg/kg); 3) vancomycin + tPA (0.9 mg/kg); 4) vancomycin + rifampicin + tPA or; 5) 0.9% NaCl, as a seven-day treatment. Hereafter, the rats were euthanized, and implants and organs were harvested for CFU enumeration. Results Vancomycin and rifampicin treatment was superior compared to monotherapy with vancomycin, with a decrease in bacterial load on the prosthetics (2.89 ± 0.77, p= 0.0012, mean ± SD). Addition of tPA to antibiotic combination therapy did not show a further decrease in bacterial load (0.32±0.50, p= 0.526, mean ± SD), however, we saw a 16% cure rate in the vancomycin + rifampicin vs. 40% cure rate in the vancomycin + rifampicin + tPA group. Whilst interesting, this trend was at our sample size not significant (p=0.24, Fisher’s exact test. Conclusions This study is the first to treat PVGI in an in vivo model, with clinically relevant doses of a fibrinolytic drug in conjunction with antibiotics. Our model could be used as a basis for future testing of both current antibiotics against PVGI and novel compounds against biofilm producing bacteria. The study drug combinations had limited effect at our samples size, and animal studies on a larger scale are therefore needed to evaluate the potential of this combination against PVGI.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Johansen, Mikkel Illemann","Rahbek, Søren Jensen","Jensen-Fangel, Søren","Larsen, Ole Halfdan","Erikstrup, Lise Tornvig","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-220050"],"event":{"end":"2021-07-12","start":"2021-07-09","title":"31st European Congress of Clinical Microbiology &amp; Infectious Diseases (ECCMID)","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Johansen, Mikkel Illemann"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fibrinolytic and antibiotic treatment of prosthetic vascular graft infections in a novel rat model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-220050","ids":["au-9f47fe18-228e-4c52-98d8-adab50540619"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-60457228F6EBD8592749A862AC35E61F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Illemann","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"521aaf8b-4d7a-4672-82c4-2c79a297b02a","name":"Johansen, Mikkel Illemann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Jensen","key":"rahbekpau","last":"Rahbek","locid":"fda9fd05-4798-4ec6-b8a9-53df61853087","name":"Rahbek, Søren Jensen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"jensenfangelpau","last":"Jensen-Fangel","locid":"9822ac67-91e2-4c70-be62-1d560c6e4ba6","name":"Jensen-Fangel, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Halfdan","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f280dbc7-1019-42be-badb-da94300ffabd","name":"Larsen, Ole Halfdan","orcid":"0000-0001-5213-7349","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise Tornvig","key":"erikstruppau","last":"Erikstrup","locid":"5313d67d-7d72-4a11-b998-2c0a51ec9612","name":"Erikstrup, Lise Tornvig","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9f47fe18-228e-4c52-98d8-adab50540619"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fibrinolytic and Antibiotic Treatment of Prosthetic Vascular Graft Infections in a Novel Rat Model","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220050","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Nordic countries share fairly similar food culture and geographical location as well as common nutrition recommendations. The aim of this paper was to review the latest data on vitamin D status and intake and to describe the national supplementation and food fortification policies to achieve adequate vitamin D intake in the Nordic countries. Methods: The data are based on results derived from a literature search presented in a workshop held in Helsinki in November 2018 and completed by recent studies. Results: Vitamin D policies and the implementation of the recommendations differ among the Nordic countries. Vitamin D fortification policies can be mandatory or voluntary and widespread, moderate or non-existent. Vitamin D supplementation recommendations differ, ranging from all age groups being advised to take supplements to only infants. In the general adult population of the Nordic countries, vitamin D status and intake are better than in the risk groups that are not consuming vitamin D supplements or foods containing vitamin D. Non-Western immigrant populations in all Nordic countries share the problem of vitamin D insufficiency and deficiency. Conclusions: Despite the common nutrition recommendations, there are differences between the Nordic countries in the implementation of the recommendations and policies to achieve adequate vitamin D intake and status. There is a need for wider Nordic collaboration studies as well as strategies to improve vitamin D status, especially in risk groups.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Itkonen, Suvi T.","Andersen, Rikke","Björk, Anne K.","Brugård Konde, Åsa","Eneroth, Hanna","Erkkola, Maijaliisa","Holvik, Kristin","Madar, Ahmed A","Meyer, Haakon E.","Tetens, Inge","Torfadóttir, Jóhanna E","Thórisdóttir, Birna","Lamberg-Allardt, Christel J. E."],"cuid":["S02-084.55-034385"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Itkonen, Suvi T."],"country":["Finland","Iceland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Food Agency","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","University of Helsinki","University of Iceland","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["25 hydroxyvitamin D","Faculty of Science","Implementation","Nordic","Nutrition","Nutrition recommendations","Policy","Vitamin D","Vitamin D fortification","Vitamin D intake","Vitamin D status"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Science Division, National Food Agency, Uppsala, Sweden."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vitamin d status and current policies to achieve adequate vitamin d intake in the nordic countries","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260035005/Itkonen_et_al_2020_Vitamin_D_status_and_current_policies_in_Nordic_countries_Accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-084.55-034385","identifier":[{"id":"31916497","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077685212","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-501c4e3a-c51c-4b0e-be2d-990e69de5b0e","ku-1e9e5927-7135-4637-b183-f6b961cf2d14"],"keyword":["25-hydroxyvitamin D","Faculty of Science","Implementation","Nordic","Nutrition","Nutrition recommendations","Policy","Vitamin D","Vitamin D fortification","Vitamin D intake","Vitamin D status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B0D8404A1FB2C583F52095748522439B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260035005/Itkonen_et_al_2020_Vitamin_D_status_and_current_policies_in_Nordic_countries_Accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203863219/1403494819896878.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Risk Benefit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"national food agency","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"National Food Agency","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Science Division, National Food Agency, Uppsala, Sweden."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute of public health","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute of Public Health","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn"