 Directed Development of Non‐Organic Catalysts with Apparent Pan‐Enzymatic Mimicry into Nanozymes for Efficient Prodrug Conversion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-148310","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Fouling is a major concern for solid/liquid interfaces of materials used in different applications. One approach of fouling control is the use of hydrophilic polymer coatings made from poly-anions and poly-cations using the layer-by-layer (LBL) method. The authors hypothesized that the poly-anionic properties and the poly-phosphate backbone of DNA would provide anti-biofouling and anti-scaling properties. To this end, poly(ethyleneimine)/DNA LBL coatings against microbial and inorganic fouling were developed, characterized and evaluated. DNA LBL coatings reduced inorganic fouling from tap water by 90% when incubated statically or under flow conditions mimicking surfaces in heat exchangers. The coatings also impaired biofilm formation by 93% on stainless steel from tap water, and resulted in a 97% lower adhesion force and reduced initial attachment of the human pathogens Staphylococcus aureus, Staphylococcus epidermidis and Pseudomonas aeruginosa on glass. This study demonstrates a proof of concept that LBL coatings with poly-anions harboring phosphate groups can address fouling in several applications.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","Zeng, Guanghong","Aslan, Hüsnü","Friis, Jakob Ege","Iruthayaraj, Joseph","Zelikin, Alexander N.","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164365"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"keyword":["Antifouling","Biofilms","Biofouling","Calcite","Calcium carbonate","DNA","Heat exchangers","Scaling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antifouling properties of layer by layer dna coatings","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85062438772","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164365","identifier":[{"id":"30821496","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85062438772","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3d7ce3b3-8157-436b-b83d-6f2ce004de97"],"keyword":["Biofouling","DNA","antifouling","biofilms","calcite","calcium carbonate","heat exchangers","scaling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2913D40A9E562A45241C7829560B02FC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guruprakash","key":"subbiahdosspau","last":"Subbiahdoss","locid":"fe2008fb-b52d-4cba-9fe7-e09a24be1112","name":"Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghong","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","locid":"41d64164-8293-4f51-b1b8-96ac2ccc6db5","name":"Zeng, Guanghong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hüsnü","key":"aslanpau","last":"Aslan","locid":"05e8885e-db36-4f96-8ecf-5263c578def8","name":"Aslan, Hüsnü","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"egefriispau","last":"Ege Friis","locid":"45c9eb89-c80b-414d-90d5-169b9987e0ab","name":"Friis, Jakob Ege","name_org":"Ege Friis, Jakob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph","key":"iruthayarajpau","last":"Iruthayaraj","locid":"1ec438e5-042e-4bdd-9684-03e9da05e8e7","name":"Iruthayaraj, Joseph","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexander N.","key":"zelikinpau","last":"Zelikin","locid":"0554974f-a5c6-4817-9b94-19e0bdc178e2","name":"Zelikin, Alexander N.","orcid":"0000-0002-9864-321X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30821496"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08927014.2019.1568417","issn":["08927014","10267867"],"issn_org":["08927014"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biofouling","pages":"75-88","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Biofouling","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062438772"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3d7ce3b3-8157-436b-b83d-6f2ce004de97"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Antifouling properties of layer by layer DNA coatings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-164365","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Khateb, Heba","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Sutherland, Duncan S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-185842"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"staphylococcus aureus adhesion to nanostructured topographies","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-185842","ids":["au-62f8d66c-449d-4b9f-a940-1c01f4b90866"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1C5F2B2C32AC672AA09EBA6BE46AD98B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heba","key":"khatebpau","last":"Khateb","locid":"d98c6ee8-14ca-4dd9-afbb-71f6f71bed40","name":"Khateb, Heba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Duncan S","key":"sutherlandpau","last":"Sutherland","locid":"5c5c563f-ca05-4219-b60d-8a3d6303ff2f","name":"Sutherland, Duncan S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"u"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Unpublished"]},"sid":["au-62f8d66c-449d-4b9f-a940-1c01f4b90866"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Staphylococcus aureus adhesion to nanostructured topographies.","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-185842","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This project aims to develop three e-learning courses, each containing six modules concerning early childhood education and care (ECEC). Each of the modules is designed to be completed in small gaps of time by educators, who have limited access to computers in their daily practice. This is one of the challenges in designing materials for educators in this area. Another challenge that also needs to be addressed when developing a learning design framework and producing modules is the diversity of educational provision across countries. Preliminary findings have revealed challenges in the academic process of condensing and re-mediating theoretical work on Child-centeredness in ECEC settings into meaningful online modules for practitioners. Difficulties can also arise when attempting to ensure coherence and progression between online modules that have been created by different partners. This presentation will emphasize how the project is developing manageable online courses for ECEC educators, which can be, completed in short spaces of time in their daily practice. Based on the experiences of re-mediating theoretical texts in multimodal formats, this paper and poster seek to encourage interest in the design process of online courses.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Buus, Lillian","Pilgaard, Michal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-658640"],"event":{"end":"2019-11-08","place":"København, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"The European Conference on e-Learning","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["E learning"],"level":"sci","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges in designing e learning to educators with limited time and access","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.via.dk/ws/files/67844294/Text.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-658640","ids":["via-83ec1116-4a61-4153-b241-0ea7a32fda87"],"keyword":["e-learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F92594249C01757C91B55C829973A5E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.via.dk/ws/files/67844294/Text.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Efter- og videreuddannelse og digitalisering, Efter- og videreuddannelse","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Pædagogik og dannelse","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, The Research Program for Learning and Digital Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lillian","key":"buuspau","last":"Buus","locid":"ff4d1a1a-32a2-4e11-8955-5da5c5f97347","name":"Buus, Lillian","orcid":"0000-0003-2367-9223","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michal","key":"pilgaardpau","last":"Pilgaard","locid":"2d8d8b95-08e2-4cd1-847d-e8785a2b1510","name":"Pilgaard, Michal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.059","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"place":"Kidmore End","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning (ECEL19)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077511201"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-83ec1116-4a61-4153-b241-0ea7a32fda87"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Challenges in Designing E-learning to Educators with Limited Time and Access","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-658640","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To identify, synthesize, and evaluate existing literature concerning the process of becoming a user of assistive technology (AT). METHOD: A systematic review and meta-synthesis were carried out. Five bibliographic databases (MEDLINE via PubMed, CINAHL, Web of Science, PsycINFO and SocINDEX) were systematically searched up to 13th of March 2017, using two sets of search terms: (i) elderly and synonyms and (ii) assistive technology and similar words, and combined with a qualitative research filter. Articles were screened, read and critically assessed. The meta-synthesis was guided by Ricoeur's theory of interpretation. RESULTS: Seventeen out of 4645 articles were included. Five phases emerged relating to the process of becoming a user of AT: phase A: Evaluating need, phase B: Acknowledging need, phase C: Incorporating the AT into daily life, phase D: Using the AT, and phase E: Future use. Three transitions, describing factors essential to moving from one phase to the next, were identified; from phase A-B: Valued activities are threatened, from phase B-C: Obtaining the AT and from phase C-D: Trust in the AT. No transition was identified from phase D-E. CONCLUSION: The meta-synthesis led to a deeper understanding of the process of older adults becoming users of AT, by exploring findings across the included articles. The identified phases and transitions in the systematic review serve as an analytical framework for understanding the process from the older adult's perspective. This review advocates for using a client-centred approach throughout the entire delivery process. Implications for rehabilitation The process of the older adult becoming a user of AT involves an individualized time factor, and this supports the practice of individualized follow-up. The process of becoming a user of AT is closely related to self-image; healthcare professionals should support not only the use of AT but also the older adult's emotional adjustment to a new self-image. The process is highly influenced by the older adult's social context; healthcare professionals should consider involving the client's social network in the AT delivery process.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Stina Meyer","Mortensen, Rikke Falgreen","Kristensen, Hanne Kaae","Hounsgaard, Lise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-048890"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Stina Meyer"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Grønlands Universitet"],"keyword":["Assistive technology","Meta synthesis","Older adults","Qualitative systematic review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Odense Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"older adults perspectives on the process of becoming users of assistive technology a qualitative systematic review and meta synthesis","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17483107.2018.1463403","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-048890","identifier":[{"id":"85065581458","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29683014","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-4bec9f1a-7edf-46b0-932b-573cba2b35a2","ucl-02fa7f90-7160-4671-9103-233cffe5536d"],"keyword":["Qualitative systematic review","assistive technology","meta-synthesis","older adults"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-305015C5A141136EBD1C8C1618E02727"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17483107.2018.1463403","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Rehabilitation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["University College Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Odense Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gl","key":"grønlands universitet","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Grønlands Universitet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Meyer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"99a0eef3-61fa-4791-89f7-dcdc4077c904","name":"Larsen, Stina Meyer","orcid":"0000-0001-5836-370X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Falgreen","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Rikke Falgreen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Kaae","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"2b8b824e-b25a-4fc1-9c9c-ec9df660ce15","name":"Kristensen, Hanne Kaae","orcid":"0000-0002-9596-5571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise","key":"hounsgaardpau","last":"Hounsgaard","locid":"b15d5b2c-4447-4a2a-918f-06e8b19f93d1","name":"Hounsga