, Research Center for VidEO: Video in Education and the learning Organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenped","last":"Ørngreen","locid":"b9c45db5-ab25-4d54-9e62-cc0bfb42ccdd","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0001-9042-3178","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mie","key":"buhlped","last":"Buhl","locid":"d50a1ab2-4c49-4e72-9a34-213eb182bc69","name":"Buhl, Mie","orcid":"0000-0002-2120-4446","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"meyerped","last":"Meyer","locid":"e0df927b-87d8-4aa1-9287-4a2b5223ae09","name":"Meyer, Bente Tobiesen","name_org":"Meyer, Bente","orcid":"0000-0003-1198-2196","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"722","place":"Reading, UK","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-891b8eef-bb21-485f-85f0-14cc7f67a51a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning : ECEL 2019 Copenhagen","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089938","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Though most teachers find formal learning activities an important part of a class visit to a science center, research shows that formal learning is seldom the outcome. Instead, school visits tend to become \"soda visits\" without preparation and learning goals, and are rarely with explicit connection to the subjects taught back in school. To accommodate these challenges at the science center Experimentarium, a partnership with University College Copenhagen was initiated in 2017. In collaboration, ten Flipped Learning based teaching materials were developed to assist visiting teachers in supporting students’ learning - before, during, and after the visit. To evaluate this intervention, a tool was developed to assess students’ learning outcomes using Personal Meaning Mapping (Falk, Moussouri and Coulson, 1998). This paper investigates and discusses this tool as an effective means for measuring ‘actual learning’ (Bundsgaard and Hansen, 2011) in contexts involving interventions aimed to integrate out-of-school visits with in-school activities. Specifically, a pre- and post-test setup was conducted in order to measure development in students conceptual understanding. Data from students’ Personal Meaning Maps were analysed quantitatively using four defined dimensions for coding: extent, breadth, depth, and mastery. The empirical data were collected from 26 students in the same class, of which 12 provided full data sets. Two central results are presented 1) the data shows development in students learning when engaging in the learning material 2) extent and breadth seem to be able to predict depth and mastery, opening up for adjustments to research method. While Personal Meaning Mapping is rather resource-intensive, and although some of these learning outcomes will remain hidden using this method, we still find it a useful and powerful tool for gaining nuanced insights into the development of students’ conceptual understanding. In conclusion, we offer some suggested modifications to the method to make it more feasible to integrate in out-of-school contexts focussing on formal learning.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Philipps, Morten Raahauge","Johannsen, Bjørn Friis","Andersen, Thomas Dyreborg","Levinsen, Henrik","Foss, Kristian Kildemoes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-387657"],"event":{"end":"2019-11-08","place":"København, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"European Conference on e-Learning","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blended learning","Method","theory practice"],"level":"sci","oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasible ways to personal meaning mapping in out of school contexts","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/67513919/Philipps_et._al._2019_Feasible_Ways_to_Personal_Meaning_Mapping_in_Out_Of_School_Contexts_ECEL19_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-387657","identifier":[{"id":"85077507463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-514942af-dc8c-4d78-81c6-de712ee71371"],"keyword":["blended learning","method","theory-practice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1A429C788D7A4F705D2B5DA6F305D027"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/67513919/Philipps_et._al._2019_Feasible_Ways_to_Personal_Meaning_Mapping_in_Out_Of_School_Contexts_ECEL19_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for læreruddannelse og livslang læring - Dekan, Digitalt kompetenceløft"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Raahauge","key":"philippspau","last":"Philipps","locid":"6825ecd7-3e66-41ab-bd90-6d95ec53048e","name":"Philipps, Morten Raahauge","orcid":"0000-0002-0569-1619","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn Friis","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","locid":"dc62d99e-7e44-46c5-b3f3-4c43882cada6","name":"Johannsen, Bjørn Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-8412-290X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Dyreborg","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"53d0dff9-7df5-47e6-9144-00a3e877da37","name":"Andersen, Thomas Dyreborg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"levinsenpau","last":"Levinsen","locid":"b848a7e4-91a0-40c6-9be2-15c74f4b92b7","name":"Levinsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-1636-7301","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Kildemoes","key":"fosspau","last":"Foss","locid":"dece4a01-f7a3-4fa0-8d49-5b540367907b","name":"Foss, Kristian Kildemoes","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.147","eisbn":["9781912764426"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"pages":"476-485","publisher":"Acpil","status":"p","subtitle":"Aalborg University, Copenhagen, Denmark. 7-8 November 2019","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077507463"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-514942af-dc8c-4d78-81c6-de712ee71371"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Feasible ways to Personal Meaning Mapping in out-of-school contexts?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-387657","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Inorganic fouling is one of the challenging problems in heat exchanger applications. One approach to mitigate fouling is to employ surface coatings. In this study, we evaluated the feasibility of surface-initiated polymerization (SIP) as thin coating technology to mitigate CaCO3 formation for heat transfer applications. The extent of formation of CaCO3 on different types of poly(oligoethyleneglycol) methacrylate brushes (POEGMA) was investigated under stagnant and flow heat-exchanging conditions. Polymer brushes of high graft density reduced the surface coverage of CaCO3more effectively than the low graft density brushes. By contrast, the thickness of the brush did not correlate with the surface coverage of CaCO3. The comparison of stagnant and flow experiments revealed that the antiscaling property of- POEGMA brushes was due to low adhesion CaCO3 deposits though the brushes themselves do not prevent the nucleation of CaCO3. b. Finally, the SIP process was successfully scaled-up to coat commercial heat exchanger plates with thickness and homogeneity comparable to lab-scale surfaces. Under industrial testing, the POEGMA brushes extended the performance by 50 h before the commencement of complete blockage.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Friis, Jakob Ege","Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","Gerved, Gorm","Holm, Allan Hjarbæk","Santos, Olga","Blichfeld, Anders Bank","Moghaddam, Saeed Zajforoushan","Thormann, Esben","Daasbjerg, Kim","Iruthayaraj, Joseph","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029596"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["Alfa Laval AB","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Aragonite","Calcite","Calcium carbonate","Heat exchangers","Inorganic fouling","POEGMA","Plate heat exchangers","Stainless steel","Surface intiated polymerization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALFA","DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ALFA","DI-PR-GFS","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of surface initiated polymer brush as anti scaling coating for plate heat exchangers","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85068745656","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Authors would like to thank Innovation Fund Denmark for financial support (Grant no. 5184-00024B ). ABB acknowledges Centre for Materials Crystallography ( DNRF93 ) and Sino-Danish Center for funding. JI, RM and KD are deeply appreciative of the generous financial support from the Danish National Research Foundation (grant no. DNRF59 ). Appendix A"],"id":"S02-100.00-029596","identifier":[{"id":"85068745656","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e9621489-1a41-4f98-9440-ce085d10f4fb","dtu-1d192910-83b0-42d2-b80c-eddd15b5434f"],"keyword":["Aragonite","Calcite","Calcium carbonate","Heat exchangers","Inorganic fouling","POEGMA","Plate heat exchangers","Stainless steel","Surface intiated polymerization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-ACB2D21B82EF783C3BEB12EE2376D75A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Plastics and Polyme