in Organic Coatings","paperid":"105196","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Progress in Organic Coatings","volume":"136"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068745656"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","Alfa Laval","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Grundfos","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","accoat a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e9621489-1a41-4f98-9440-ce085d10f4fb","dtu-1d192910-83b0-42d2-b80c-eddd15b5434f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of Surface-initiated Polymer brush as Anti-scaling Coating for Plate Heat Exchangers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-029596","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Extracellular DNA (eDNA) is an abundant matrix component that protects biofilm from environmental stress, facilitate horizontal gene transfer, and serve as a source of nutrients. eDNA is also found in Listeria monocytogenes biofilm, but it is unknown to which extent its importance as a matrix component varies in terms of phylogenetic relatedness. This study aims to determine if these variations exist. Biofilm forming capacity of ten L. monocytogenes strains of different phylogenetic lineages and serotypes was examined using crystal violet assay at 37°C and 22°C. eDNA content was evaluated fluorometrically at 37°C and at 22°C, then the 3D structure of biofilm was studied by confocal laser scanning microscopy (CLSM). Biofilm forming capacity differed significantly between the culturing conditions and was higher at 37°C than at ambient temperature. eDNA signal distribution was found to be influenced by strain and lineage. CLSM images revealed information about spatial distribution in the biofilm. The information about the eDNA spatial organisation in the biofilm contributes to the understanding of the role of eDNA in a biofilm formation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Šuláková, Martina","Pazlarová, Jarmila","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Demnerová, Kateřina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-175926"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Chemistry and Technology, Prague"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Confocal laser scanning microscopy","Extracellular DNA","Listeria"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distribution of extracellular dna in i listeria monocytogenes i biofilm","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079345134","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-175926","identifier":[{"id":"85079345134","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-51b7eaac-17a5-48d9-8f35-30aa6811d7f1"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Confocal laser scanning microscopy","Extracellular DNA","Listeria"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-AC641DE9E4A21206563550DB421C6705"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cz","key":"university of chemistry and technology prague","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Chemistry and Technology, Prague","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina","key":"šulákovápau","last":"Šuláková","name":"Šuláková, Martina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jarmila","key":"pazlarovápau","last":"Pazlarová","name":"Pazlarová, Jarmila","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kateřina","key":"demnerovápau","last":"Demnerová","name":"Demnerová, Kateřina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17221/9/2019-cjfs","issn":["12121800","18059317"],"issn_org":["12121800"],"issue":"6","journal":"Czech Journal of Food Sciences","pages":"409-416","publisher":"Czech Academy of Agricultural Sciences","status":"p","title":"Czech Journal of Food Sciences","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079345134"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-51b7eaac-17a5-48d9-8f35-30aa6811d7f1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Distribution of extracellular DNA in <i>Listeria monocytogenes</i> biofilm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-175926","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: This paper is a theoretical discussion about the extent to which school subjects can contribute to teaching students computational thinking. Or is it the other way around and, perhaps surprisingly, how computational thinking might transform existing school subjects? The discussion takes as its point of departure the national experimental project Technology Understanding, which is the Danish response to a worldwide interest in bringing digitalization to students in primary and secondary schools and the Danish governmental initiative regarding implementation of digital literacy as a new school subject and as an integrated part of existing school subjects in primary school (Ministry of Education 2018). Visual arts education is one of the subjects chosen for the integration of technology, and this paper follows up on the ministry's intention by considering visual arts as the starting point for computational thinking. At issue is how visual art may be informed by computational thinking and how computational thinking may be informed by visual art. I argue that teaching students to understand algorithms and data processes can be inspired by practices from contemporary art and the ideas of new materialism (Barad 2008). Contemporary art may be characterized as conceptual, distributive, and interventional in life practices, and programming principles may illuminate how human activities and algorithms intertwine. I also argue that the teaching of contemporary art can be inspired by principles from programming and algorithms. These practices can illuminate how artistic concepts may be planned and designed for human interaction. However, programming for contemporary art requires openness regarding use, while programming for data processes requires the opposite. Thus, the integration of computational thinking into visual arts education is more than a means for understanding programming and algorithms; the dynamic also works in reverse. This paper will bring a wider societal perspective to bear on teaching computational thinking by bringing school subjects into the center of discussions and drawing on current discussions of STEAM education and contemporary art","author_count":4,"contributors":["Buhl, Mie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059091"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Buhl, Mie"],"keyword":["Computational thinking","Contemporary arts","Technological understanding","Technology","Visual arts education"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Research Center for Visual Studies (ViLD)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational thinking utilizing visual arts or maybe the other way around","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/314904802/Computational_thinking_in_the_arts_or_art_in_computational_thinking_Published.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059091","identifier":[{"id":"85077508067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1ee9f11d-35a5-46ab-b7c0-a3d76d99848b"],"keyword":["Contemporary arts","computational thinking","technological understanding","technology","visual arts education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9E5784C105F82CFF4B4AAA8F7EB0973E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/314904802/Computational_thinking_in_the_arts_or_art_in_computational_thinking_Published.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org"