t of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, ILD-LAB – Research lab for IT and Learning Design","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, L-ILD - IT and Learning Design","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, Research Center for VidEO: Video in Education and the learning Organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpau","last":"Ørngreen","locid":"b9c45db5-ab25-4d54-9e62-cc0bfb42ccdd","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0001-9042-3178","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpau","last":"Buhl","locid":"d50a1ab2-4c49-4e72-9a34-213eb182bc69","name":"Buhl, Mie","orcid":"0000-0002-2120-4446","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"e0df927b-87d8-4aa1-9287-4a2b5223ae09","name":"Meyer, Bente Tobiesen","name_org":"Meyer, Bente","orcid":"0000-0003-1198-2196","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"place":"Reading, UK","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning ECEL: 2019 Copenhagen","volume":"2019-November"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8249ea23-5abc-4dda-a1dd-d9da625c43dd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"ECEL Preface","type":"Book Preface, Encycl. Entry","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-087935","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Advances in information, communication, technology (I.C.T) particularly the internet is driving universities worldwide into integrating technology into teaching and learning in the classrooms. Ready access to multimedia learning platforms are encouraging faculty members to move away from traditional print-based and face-to-face teaching approach into adopting blended learning. However, insufficient learner satisfaction has been noted as an obstacle in most universities. In view of this, this paper assesses the learning experience of students within a blended learning environment in a Higher Education Institution (HEIs) in Ghana Technology University College (GTUC). The driving force for this study is to enhance students’ learning experience with the use of technology within a blended learning environment. The Learning Management System (LMS) adapted to engage students within the blended learning environment is Moodle. The study employed both qualitative and quantitative methods to measure the students’ learning experience. A total of 244 respondents from three different faculties and levels offering bachelors and master’s degree were used. The study employed simple descriptive analysis and thematic analysis to measure the student's learning experience within the blended learning environment. The impression from the findings indicates that the online learning engagements enhanced the face-to-face teaching and learning and also increased retention and performance among the students. It was however noted that poor internet connectivity, reluctant of some lecturers, lack of orientation affected the effective implementation of the blended learning. More so, most of the learners affirmed that there is no clear-cut policy that enforces effective implementation of the blended learning approach in the university. The study affirmed that effective usage of blended learning approach enhances students’ learning experience in HEIs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Freeman, Emmauel","Antwi-Boampong, Ahmed","Baffoe-Kodom Agyemang, Odeneho"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-096261"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Antwi-Boampong, Ahmed","Baffoe-Kodom Agyemang, Odeneho"],"country":["Ghana","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Arden University","Ghana Communication Technology University"],"keyword":["Blended learning","Higher education institution","Learning experience","Moodle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"students learning experience within a blended learning environment in a higher education institution in ghana","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://books.google.dk/books?id=ZMjBDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA160&dq=DOI:+%2210.34190/EEL.19.117%22&hl=da&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiAi6zQydXmAhUnQ0EAHY5EBR0Q6AEIKDAA#v=onepage&q&f=false","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-096261","identifier":[{"id":"85077504480","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9f67ac9b-8318-490f-96c4-92780eb23933"],"keyword":["Blended learning","Higher education institution","Learning experience","Moodle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6C48A55ED78F79B64305588A76731EAB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gh","key":"ghana communication technology university","loc":["Ghana","Africa"],"name":"Ghana Communication Technology University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Center for Communication, Media and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"arden university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Arden University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmauel","key":"freemanpau","last":"Freeman","name":"Freeman, Emmauel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ahmed","key":"antwiboampongpau","last":"Antwi-Boampong","locid":"2b7e382a-a964-4ddd-a77c-1969d16abe35","name":"Antwi-Boampong, Ahmed","orcid":"0000-0003-2887-2807","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Odeneho","key":"baffoekodomagyemangpau","last":"Baffoe-Kodom Agyemang","name":"Baffoe-Kodom Agyemang, Odeneho","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"orngreenpedh","last":"Orngreen","name":"Orngreen, Rikke","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.117","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"160-168","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077504480"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9f67ac9b-8318-490f-96c4-92780eb23933"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Students’ Learning Experience within a Blended Learning Environment in a Higher Education Institution in Ghana","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-096261","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The paper investigates how the use of visualisations and video productions combined with peer-feedback sessions can create exploratory approaches to game design in online teaching. Thus, the paper aims to provide insights into the iterative learning processes of developing games in online game based learning. The empirical data is based on an explorative case study where master students from the international Nordic Visual Studies and Art Education (NoVA) design games as a part of an online game-based learning course. Throughout the course the students were situated at three different universities in Finland, Sweden and Denmark, collaborating cross-cultural across campuses. The purpose of the study was to explore how to establish an online space for joint design inquiry in the context of games for changes across cultural and professional barriers. The data used for analysis is teaching observations, videos of play sessions, students’ reflection papers, written and oral evaluation with participants after completion of the course. The analysis is based on different PBL activities; lectures, video tutorials, presentation- and feedback sessions, reflexive exercises and students’ self-directed design processes and learning in groups. Game theory and exercises were presented through videos and visuals to support the students’ iterative processes of developing games. Analysis of the PBL activities show how teachers’ video tutorials relating theoretical game concepts to the students’ group work supported their entrance in the game field as well as their design processes. How to balance feedback-related video tutorials and teachers’ time for preparation is identified as a relevant issue for further exploration in online game-based teaching. Findings show how the students’ visualisations and video productions exemplifying game situations, created a visible reference point for further discussions in the feedback sessions across campuses, which guided the game development. Thus, the combination of inquiry approaches, critical game theory and design processes combined with students’ visualisations and video productions indicates interesting connections for bridging gaps between professions, e.g. in art and games.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hautopp, Heidi","Ejsing-Duun, Stine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113002"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Educational design","Higher education","online game based learning","students as game designers","video productions","visualisations"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of visualisations and video productions in online game based learning","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85077506990&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113002","identifier":[{"id":"85077506990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d89e97df-4d6e-4c65-bab5-ae6d7569afdb"],"keyword":["Educational design","Higher education","online game-based learning","students as game designers","video productions","visualisations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5AAC0111BF669F40D1BF48C7A475F443"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, ILD - Forskningslab i IT og Læringsdesign (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Research Center for VidEO: Video in Education and the learning Organisation (Learning)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, ILD-LAB – Research lab for IT and Learning Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heidi","key":"hautopppau","last":"Hautopp","locid":"0993cb33-a065-4e3d-92e7-6a706904ccf6","name":"Hautopp, Heidi","orcid":"0000-0003-3567-7727","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"ejsingduunpau","last":"Ejsing-Duun","locid":"93a1ba27-980c-4370-92a4-121934a02c5a","name":"Ejsing-Duun, Stine","orcid":"0000-0001-7162-4505","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.094","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"192-199","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL","status":"p","subtitle":"Aalborg University, Copenhagen, Denmark, 7-8 November, 2019","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077506990"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d89e97df-4d6e-4c65-bab5-ae6d7569afdb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The use of visualisations and video productions in online game-based learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113002","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The Flipped Classroom (FC) is an instruction method, where “events that have traditionally taken place inside the classroom now take place outside and vice versa”, which has known a significant surge of popularity in the past decade. In FCs, different types of activities may take place depending on the session type (pre-class, in-class, or after-class), the learning objectives to fulfil, the type and size of the class, the available infrastructure, the time available etc. In order to support the activities taking place in FCs, instructors can use various technological tools and online environment, especially to support the preparation of students before class. A marked recent trend in the FC is the increased use of Learning Analytics (LA) to support the development of the FC and students’ reflexive learning. However, there has been no systematic investigation into combining LA and the FC, and it appeared that there was a lack of research on the issue. The aim of this paper is to investigate the literature on applications of LA in FCs, and to determine the best practices and needs for technological development supporting LA in the FC. In order to perform this study, we did a scoping review of literature in the subject to determine research trends in the use of LA in the FC. We conclude that there is great potential to use LA in the FC, and try to project where further research is heading.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Algayres, Muriel Gaelle","Triantafyllou, Evangelia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118572"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"online environments for supporting learning analytics in the flipped classroom a scoping review","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.academic-conferences.org/wp-content/uploads/dlm_uploads/2019/11/ECEL-Abstract-Booklet-Embedded.pdf#pages=47","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/335383187/ECEL19_EEL_063_camera_ready.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-118572","identifier":[{"id":"85077506353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ebcb736d-516d-4c8e-b785-7d421e90a5fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C7D055FE2250A5E0C899AD152745C3AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.academic-conferences.org/wp-content/uploads/dlm_uploads/2019/11/ECEL-Abstract-Booklet-Embedded.pdf#pages=47","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/335383187/ECEL19_EEL_063_camera_ready.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Muriel Gaelle","key":"algayrespau","last":"Algayres","locid":"a5423a18-8357-4c1c-963c-ed57c985bdfd","name":"Algayres, Muriel Gaelle","orcid":"0000-0002-5572-356X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evangelia","key":"triantafylloupau","last":"Triantafyllou","locid":"7129c2da-47d0-4d2c-90fd-3897b5d4ef1e","name":"Triantafyllou, Evangelia","orcid":"0000-0001-8764-2118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.063","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"16-23","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning (ECEL 2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077506353"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ebcb736d-516d-4c8e-b785-7d421e90a5fb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Online environments for supporting learning analytics in the flipped classroom : a scoping review","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118572","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Iron-containing metallic implants are shown herein to mediate hydrolysis of glycosidic linkages. Using glucuronide prodrugs for broad-spectrum fluoroquinolone antibacterial agents, we capitalize on this behaviour and perform localized synthesis of antimicrobials which affords a significant zone of inhibition of bacterial growth around the metallic material.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Meer, Marja Ter","Dillion, Ross","Nielsen, Signe Maria","Walther, Raoul","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Daamen, Willeke F.","Van Den Heuvel, Lambertus P.","Van Der Vliet, J. Adam","Lomme, Roger M.L.M.","Hoogeveen, Yvonne L.","Schultze Kool, Leo J.","Schaffer, Jeremy E.","Zelikin, Alexander N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256949"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Meer, Marja Ter"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innate glycosidic activity in metallic implants for localized synthesis of antibacterial drugs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85059500734","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256949","identifier":[{"id":"85059500734","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30489589","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-df8941a9-f777-455f-8db5-915e0fc48b98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-92776F54B72E0F27C5AF980B46FCB7C4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nij