{"abstract":"This paper assesses the teaching and learning experiences of faculty understanding of blending learning in a Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) in Ghana. The driving force for this paper is the transformational agenda of most HEIs to integrate technology with teaching and learning. The study posits that the adoption of blended learning for teaching and learning by faculty members in HEIs interplay with external and internal factors within and without the universities. Nonetheless, blended learning approaches in teaching boils down to motivation as the core concern around which these afore mentioned factors revolve. The experiences of fifteen faculty members using blended learning at the Ghana Technology University College was analysed using Thematic Analysis and Grounded Theory to develop a BL model. The paper describes the faculty blended learning adoption model and explains the model constructs and their relationships. The study indicated that staff motivation is at the core of the emergent theory of faculty adoption and presents institutional readiness, faculty technology affinity, student disposition to adopt blended learning and pedagogy fitness as constructs within and without the blended learning environment which positively influences faculty to adopt blended learning for teaching and learning.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Antwi-Boampong, Ahmed","Freeman, Emmanuel","Muat, HANNAH"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100544"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"corresponding_author":["Freeman, Emmanuel","Muat, HANNAH"],"country":["Ghana"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghana Communication Technology University","University for Development Studies"],"keyword":["Blended learning","Faculty adoption","Grounded theory","Higher education institutions","Thematic analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a thematic and grounded theory understanding of faculty adoption of blended learning in higher education","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://books.google.dk/books?id=ZMjBDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA160&dq=DOI:+%2210.34190/EEL.19.117%22&hl=da&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiAi6zQydXmAhUnQ0EAHY5EBR0Q6AEIKDAA#v=onepage&q&f=false","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-100544","identifier":[{"id":"85077501679","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ae10a121-2889-4b5a-9090-87e706eab9ff"],"keyword":["Blended learning","Faculty adoption","Grounded theory","Higher education institutions","Thematic analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E787F4757C27F4C0F8E9C3A0E29D0DD4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Center for Communication, Media and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gh","key":"ghana communication technology university","loc":["Ghana","Africa"],"name":"Ghana Communication Technology University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gh","key":"university for development studies","loc":["Ghana","Africa"],"name":"University for Development Studies","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ahmed","key":"antwiboampongpau","last":"Antwi-Boampong","locid":"2b7e382a-a964-4ddd-a77c-1969d16abe35","name":"Antwi-Boampong, Ahmed","orcid":"0000-0003-2887-2807","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanuel","key":"freemanpau","last":"Freeman","name":"Freeman, Emmanuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"HANNAH","key":"muatpau","last":"Muat","name":"Muat, HANNAH","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"orngreenpedh","last":"Orngreen","name":"Orngreen, Rikke","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.112","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"621-628","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077501679"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ae10a121-2889-4b5a-9090-87e706eab9ff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Thematic and Grounded Theory Understanding of Faculty Adoption of Blended Learning in Higher Education","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-100544","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Treatment of polymicrobial infections requires combination therapy with drugs that have different antimicrobial spectra and possibly work in synergy. However, the different pharmacokinetics and adverse side effects challenge the simultaneous delivery of multiple drugs at the appropriate concentrations to the site of infection. Formulation of multiple drugs in nano-carrier systems may improve therapeutic efficacy by increasing the local concentration and lowering the systemic concentration, leading to fewer side effects. In this study, we loaded polymyxin B and vancomycin on bare and carboxyl-modified mesoporous silica nanoparticles (B-MSNs and CMSNs, respectively) to achieve simulataneous local delivery of antibiotics against Gram-positive and –negative bacteria. Polymyxin B adsorbed preferentially to nanoparticles compared to vancomycin. The total antibiotic loading was 563 μg and 453 μg per mg B-MSNs or C-MSNs, respectively. Both B-MSNs and C-MSNs loaded with antibiotics were effective against Gram-negative and Gram-positive bacteria. The antibiotics had synergistic interactions against Gram-negative bacteria, and the antimicrobial efficacy was higher for antibiotic-loaded CMSNs compared to free antibiotics at the same concentration even though the cytotoxicity was lower. Our study shows that formulations of existing antibiotics in nanocarrier systems can improve their therapeutic efficiency, indicating that combination therapy with drug-loaded silica nanoparticles may provide a better treatment outcome for infections that require high concentrations of multiple drugs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gounani, Zahra","Asadollahi, Mohammad A.","Pedersen, Jannik Nedergaard","Lyngsø, Jeppe","Pedersen, Jan Skov","Arpanaei, Ayyoob","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-192327"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institute for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology Iran","University of Isfahan"],"keyword":["Acinetobacter baumannii","Antibacterial activity","Delivery","Drug delivery","Mesoporous silica nanoparticles","Nanofibers","Polymyxin B","Pore size","Vancomycin","X ray scattering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mesoporous silica nanoparticles carrying multiple antibiotics provide enhanced synergistic effect and improved biocompatibility","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85058442685","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-192327","identifier":[{"id":"30572158","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000459837800057","type":"wos"},{"id":"85058442685","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6e6892ff-db00-4098-8f48-d38c880bbff6"],"keyword":["ACINETOBACTER-BAUMANNII","ANTIBACTERIAL ACTIVITY","COLISTIN COMBINATION","DELIVERY","Drug delivery","Mesoporous silica nanoparticles","NANOFIBERS","PORE-SIZE","Polymyxin B","RESISTANT STRAINS","Vancomycin","X-RAY-SCATTERING"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C77044569A8B822FF178478FE1723B86"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"national institute for genetic engineering and biotechnology iran","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"National Institute for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology Iran","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ir","key":"university of isfahan","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"University of Isfahan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zahra","key":"gounanizahrapau","last":"Gounani","locid":"b1f6af35-04d3-4ac3-954e-6c19fb039ec9","name":"Gounani, Zahra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad A.","key":"asadollahimohammadapau","last":"Asadollahi","name":"Asadollahi, Mohammad A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik Nedergaard","key":"pedersenjanniknedergaardpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9afe60ea-968a-49aa-81d4-859eb80d7b15","name":"Pedersen, Jannik Nedergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe","key":"lyngsøjeppepau","last":"Lyngsø","locid":"c8a7fe42-fe44-4dab-98d8-58eb73f245d4","name":"Lyngsø, Jeppe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Skov","key":"pedersenjanskovpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8cb5e42a-3881-479c-82a5-232355605d7e","name":"Pedersen, Jan Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-7768-0206","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ayyoob","key":"arpanaeiayyoobpau","last":"Arpanaei","name":"Arpanaei, Ayyoob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30572158"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.colsurfb.2018.12.035","issn":["09277765","18734367"],"issn_org":["09277765"],"journal":"Colloids and Surfaces B: Biointerfaces","pages":"498-508","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Colloids and Surfaces B: Biointerfaces","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058442685"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6e6892ff-db00-4098-8f48-d38c880bbff6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mesoporous silica nanoparticles carrying multiple antibiotics provide enhanced synergistic effect and improved biocompatibility","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192327","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this work, the effects of various factors, including the ultrasonic duty cycle and intensity of ultrasonic irradiation, ultrasonication and clove oil content in production of clove oil nanoemulsion were investigated. In preparation of nanoemulsion Tween® 80/Span® 80 as nonionic surfactants via ultrasonic emulsification method was used. The average droplets size of clove oil nanoemulsion decreased with an increase in duty cycle; whereas pulsed ultrasound with proper intervals was more efficient than continuous ultrasonication. In order to replace the use of organic solvent and increase the dispersity of active ingredient, suitable emulsifiers were used. The nanopesticides made by ultrasound at optimum formula conditions were defined at ultrasonication time of 300s, surfactants concentration of 5wt%, hydrophilic-lipophilic balance number of 9, duty cycle 0.75% and ultrasonic intensity 208W/cm2. The stability of droplets size of nanoemulsions for duration of 6months was evaluated. Stable nanoemulsion clove oil with 10wt% of clove oil content was formulated at optimum conditions with average droplets size around 43nm at the beginning and after 6months nanoemulsions re-sized and it was around 100nm. A stable nanoemulsion of clove oil in water with suitable droplets size as a nanopesticide was prepared.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shahavi, Mohammad Hassan","Hosseini, Morteza","Jahanshahi, Mohsen","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Darzi, Ghasem Najafpour"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-195563"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Darzi, Ghasem Najafpour"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Babol Noshirvani University of Technology"],"keyword":["Clove oil","Nanoemulsion","Oil in water emulsion","Ultrasonication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of critical parameters for preparation of stable clove oil nanoemulsion","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84941007233","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-195563","identifier":[{"id":"84941007233","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-740a5244-e223-4ab1-9e33-928a86a52c02"],"keyword":["Clove oil","Nanoemulsion","Nonionic surfactants","Oil in water emulsion","Ultrasonication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6550B1A50E8FF3771B4204A20F6D2B81"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"babol noshirvani university of technology","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Babol Noshirvani University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Hassan","key":"shahavipau","last":"Shahavi","locid":"81fde6d0-7738-41cd-b950-f75cded3840d","name":"Shahavi, Mohammad Hassan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morteza","key":"hosseinipau","last":"Hosseini","name":"Hosseini, Morteza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"jahanshahipau","last":"Jahanshahi","name":"Jahanshahi, Mohsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ghasem Najafpour","key":"darzipau","last":"Darzi","name":"Darzi, Ghasem Najafpour","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.arabjc.2015.08.024","issn":["18785352"],"issue":"8","journal":"Arabian Journal of Chemistry","pages":"3225-3230","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Arabian Journal of Chemistry","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941007233"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-740a5244-e223-4ab1-9e33-928a86a52c02"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Evaluation of critical parameters for preparation of stable clove oil nanoemulsion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-195563","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In response to the common but often overlooked challenges faced by many teaching professionals when having to move from a face-to-face model of teaching and learning to blended learning (BL), the purpose of this paper is to present a series of research-based and practical guidelines to support educators facing this transition. Some of the key issues discussed are the need for an openness-to-change mindset, the importance of a meaningful integration between face-to-face and online elements and the need for a conscious choice of technology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lopez, Nuria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-290985"],"event":{"acronym":"ECEL","end":"2019-11-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-11-07","title":"18th European Conference on e-Learning. ECEL 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blended learning","Constructive alignment","Curriculum design","SAMR model","Teaching presence","Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the climb to the blended learning peak","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-290985","identifier":[{"id":"85077510361","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-a3bc82d8-82c7-4523-9960-1a817e9c066a"],"keyword":["Blended learning","Constructive alignment","Curriculum design","SAMR model","Teaching presence","Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-35F4901E5428D660EF18723F0AE905D6"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of International Economics, Government and Business"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nuria","key":"lopezpau","last":"Lopez","name":"Lopez, Nuria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"ørngreenpedh","last":"Ørngreen","name":"Ørngreen, Rikke","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mie","key":"buhlpedh","last":"Buhl","name":"Buhl, Mie","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bente","key":"meyerpedh","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Bente","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/eel.19.034","eisbn":["9781912764419"],"isbn":["9781912764426"],"issn":["20488637"],"pages":"665-667","place":"Reading","publisher":"Academic Conferences and Publishing International","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on e-Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 18th European Conference on e-Learning, ECEL 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077510361"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-a3bc82d8-82c7-4523-9960-1a817e9c066a"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Climb to the Blended Learning Peak","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-290985","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bacteria from the candidate phylum Acetothermia (OP1) are globally dispersed and occupy many diverse habitats (see figure to the right). However, little is known about their physiology and ecology. We previously observed that Acetothermia bacteria were the most abundant bacteria in the metagenome from an anaerobic digester. Aim: To learn more about their abundance, morphology, and physiological and ecological function.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hao, Liping","McIlroy, Simon Jon","Kirkegaard, Rasmus Hansen","Karst, Søren Michael","Warnakulasuriya, Eustace Yrosh Fernando","Aslan, Hüsnü","Meyer, Rikke","Albertsen, Mads","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Dueholm, Morten Simonsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115248"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-17","place":"Leipzig, de","start":"2018-08-12","title":"17th International Symposium on Microbial Ecology","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bacteria","Microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of bipolar prosthecae by candidate phylum acetothermia bacteria","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/303628871/180912_ISME17_poster4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-115248","ids":["aau-e03a57aa-7d64-480a-93cf-a10c157414c9"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A39E14D1C21348E09676E75A02BB8C67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/303628871/180912_ISME17_poster4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Bioscience and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liping","key":"haopau","last":"Hao","locid":"6c51d5ec-6477-4465-b266-40665aaaf50a","name":"Hao, Liping","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Jon","key":"mcilroypau","last":"McIlroy","locid":"9309e11f-d9f7-4ef8-9bfe-182dd6435712","name":"McIlroy, Simon Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-3749-8730","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Hansen","key":"kirkegaardpau","last":"Kirkegaard","locid":"d5c8fdb2-a72d-47fa-b22a-5647cef23c40","name":"Kirkegaard, Rasmus Hansen","orcid":"0000-0003-3349-3617","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Michael","key":"karstpau","last":"Karst","locid":"73f48fd9-cb58-4023-ab8a-b4f734cf7bcb","name":"Karst, Søren Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-0233-160X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eustace","key":"fernandopau","last":"Fernando","locid":"c22a861f-697d-46d2-ba5e-7820ab34d3e0","name":"Warnakulasuriya, Eustace Yrosh Fernando","name_org":"Fernando, Eustace","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hüsnü","key":"aslanpau","last":"Aslan","name":"Aslan, Hüsnü","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Rikke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"albertsenpau","last":"Albertsen","locid":"6c728ec9-5a0d-40c7-b3f3-1741c6e01ccc","name":"Albertsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-6151-190X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per Halkjær","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8321dd0d-5e0c-4334-81a7-ece0b4b66f4c","name":"Nielsen, Per Halkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-6402-1877","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Simonsen","key":"dueholmpau","last":"Dueholm","locid":"0824b5d0-8995-42b9-9df4-6e9996430c39","name":"Dueholm, Morten Simonsen","orcid":"0000-0003-4135-2670","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e03a57aa-7d64-480a-93cf-a10c157414c9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Development of bipolar prosthecae by candidate phylum Acetothermia bacteria","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115248","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Bacterial contamination of implantable biomaterials is a significant socioeconomic and healthcare burden. Indeed, bacterial colonization of implants after surgery has a high rate of incidence whereas concurrent prophylaxis using systemic antibiotics has limited clinical success. In this work, we develop enzyme-prodrug therapy (EPT) to prevent and to treat bacteria at interfaces. Towards the overall goal, novel prodrugs for fluoroquinolone antibiotics were developed on a privileged glucuronide scaffold. Whereas carbamoyl prodrugs were not stable and not suitable for EPT, glucuronides containing self-immolative linker between glucuronic acid masking group and the antibiotic were stable in solution and readily underwent bioconversion in the presence of β-glucuronidase. Surface coatings for model biomaterials were engineered using sequential polymer deposition technique. Resulting coatings afforded fast prodrug conversion and mediated antibacterial measures against planktonic species as evidenced by pronounced zone of bacterial growth inhibition around the biomaterial surface. These biomaterials coupled with the glucuronide prodrugs also effectively combatted bacteria within established biofilms and also successfully prevented bacterial colonization of the surface. To our knowledge, this is the first report of EPT engineered to the surface of biomaterials to mediate antibacterial measures.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Walther, Raoul","Nielsen, Signe Maria","Christiansen, Rikke","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Zelikin, Alexander N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164648"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Biomaterial","Enzyme prodrug therapy","Glucuronide","Prodrug"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combatting implant associated biofilms through localized drug synthesis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85052228862","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164648","identifier":[{"id":"30138714","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6176123","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85052228862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3e01125b-d714-40c3-b1b1-84e5032d08df"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Biomaterial","Enzyme-prodrug therapy","Glucuronide","Prodrug"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F7D3DF12AF29AA5EF4F24832013881E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raoul","key":"waltherpau","last":"Walther","locid":"994eba41-cfe2-44bb-9280-b648f7292d72","name":"Walther, Raoul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Maria","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Signe Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"8cebe235-15bb-40cf-afde-46d0a64a86fb","name":"Christiansen, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alexander N.","key":"zelikinpau","last":"Zelikin","locid":"0554974f-a5c6-4817-9b94-19e0bdc178e2","name":"Zelikin, Alexander N.","orcid":"0000-0002-9864-321X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30138714"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jconrel.2018.08.025","issn":["01683659","18734995"],"issn_org":["01683659"],"journal":"Journal of Controlled Release","pages":"94-102","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Controlled Release","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052228862"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3e01125b-d714-40c3-b1b1-84e5032d08df"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Combatting implant-associated biofilms through localized drug synthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-164648","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Finegoldia magna, a Gram-positive anaerobic coccus, is an opportunistic pathogen, associated with medical device-related infections. F. magna is the only described species of the genus Finegoldia. We report the analysis of 17 genomes of Finegoldia isolates. Phylogenomic analyses showed that the Finegoldia population can be divided into two distinct clades, with an average nucleotide identity of 90.7%. One clade contains strains of F. magna, whereas the other clade includes more heterogeneous strains, hereafter tentatively named \"Finegoldia nericia\". The latter species appears to be more abundant in the human microbiome. Surface structure differences between strains of F. magna and \"F. nericia\" were detected by microscopy. Strain-specific heterogeneity is high and previously identified host-interacting factors are present only in subsets of \"F. nericia\" and F. magna strains. However, all genomes encode multiple host factor-binding proteins such as albumin-, collagen-, and immunoglobulin-binding proteins, and two to four copies of CAMP (Christie-Atkins-Munch-Petersen) factors; in accordance, most strains show a positive CAMP reaction for co-hemolysis. Our work sheds new light of the genus Finegoldia and its ability to bind host components. Future research should explore if the genomic differences identified here affect the potential of different Finegoldia species and strains to cause opportunistic infections.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Brüggemann, Holger","Jensen, Anders","Nazipi, Seven","Aslan, Hüsnü","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Poehlein, Anja","Brzuszkiewicz, Elzbieta","Al-Zeer, Munir A","Brinkmann, Volker","Söderquist, Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-271104"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Infection Biology","Technical University of Berlin","University of Göttingen","Örebro University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pan genome analysis of the genus finegoldia identifies two distinct clades strain specific heterogeneity and putative virulence factors","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85040467514","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-271104","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5762925","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29321635","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040467514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f889ea41-584a-4d09-80e4-064354a70ac6"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CC972F50158652A762C75539842DD497"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for infection biology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Infection Biology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"örebro university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Örebro University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger","key":"brüggemannpau","last":"Brüggemann","locid":"029d7735-40a7-4a8f-a552-67e496015144","name":"Brüggemann, Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-7433-0190","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"294ed818-d0c3-4397-928c-bb5218f288da","name":"Jensen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Seven","key":"nazipipau","last":"Nazipi","locid":"95452590-bd27-4fdd-a370-cd1e79a47184","name":"Nazipi, Seven","orcid":"0000-0002-4702-2691","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hüsnü","key":"aslanpau","last":"Aslan","locid":"05e8885e-db36-4f96-8ecf-5263c578def8","name":"Aslan, Hüsnü","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"poehleinpau","last":"Poehlein","name":"Poehlein, Anja","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elzbieta","key":"brzuszkiewiczpau","last":"Brzuszkiewicz","name":"Brzuszkiewicz, Elzbieta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Munir A","key":"alzeerpau","last":"Al-Zeer","name":"Al-Zeer, Munir A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"brinkmannpau","last":"Brinkmann","name":"Brinkmann, Volker","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"söderquistpau","last":"Söderquist","name":"Söderquist, Bo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29321635"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-18661-8","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"266","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040467514"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f889ea41-584a-4d09-80e4-064354a70ac6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pan-genome analysis of the genus Finegoldia identifies two distinct clades, strain-specific heterogeneity, and putative virulence factors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-271104","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Bacillus cereus is one of the most common opportunistic pathogens causing foodborne illness, as well as a common source of contamination in the dairy industry. B. cereus can form robust biofilms on food processing surfaces, resulting in food contamination due to shedding of cells and spores. Despite the medical and industrial relevance of this species, the genetic basis of biofilm formation in B. cereus is not well studied. In order to identify genes required for biofilm formation in this bacterium, we created a library of 5000 + transposon mutants of the biofilm-forming strain B. cereusATCC 10987, using an unbiased mariner transposon approach. The mutant library was screened for the ability to form a pellicle biofilm at the air-media interface, as well as a submerged biofilm at the solid-media interface. A total of 91 genes were identified as essential for biofilm formation. These genes encode functions such as chemotaxis, amino acid metabolism and cellular repair mechanisms, and include numerous genes not previously known to be required for biofilm formation. Although the majority of disrupted genes are not directly responsible for motility, further investigations revealed that the vast majority of the biofilm-deficient mutants were also motility impaired. This observation implicates motility as a pivotal factor in the formation of a biofilm by B. cereus. These results expand our knowledge of the fundamental molecular mechanisms of biofilm formation by B. cereus.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Okshevsky, Mira Ursula","Rasmussen, Matilde Greve","Otero Lamela, Elena","Nilsson, Martin","Tolker-Nielsen, Tim","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S02-098.33-018825"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bacillus cereus","Biofilm","Motility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a transposon mutant library of i bacillus cereus i atcc 000000010987 reveals novel genes required for biofilm formation and implicates motility as an important factor for pellicle biofilm formation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mbo3.552","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.33-018825","identifier":[{"id":"29164822","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85034786508","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5911993","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-5493a809-0722-4a07-b777-2239920f476a","ku-85055aac-7bcd-45d4-98b1-db7628d5d2ed"],"keyword":["Bacillus cereus","Biofilm","Biofilm extracellular matrix","Motility","dlt operon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EC8340586DCA588170B8BD4B646F7D10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/127489278/Okshevsky_et_al_2018_MicrobiologyOpen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mbo3.552","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/215979264/Okshevsky_et_al_2018_MicrobiologyOpen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mira Ursula","key":"okshevskypau","last":"Okshevsky","locid":"70b6699e-a3fc-49e2-9052-08c02dfa5bae","name":"Okshevsky, Mira Ursula","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matilde Greve","key":"louwpau","last":"Louw","locid":"a3f5c50e-4c0a-47ee-aa5d-f0cc7ec7d07c","name":"Rasmussen, Matilde Greve","name_org":"Louw, Matilde Greve","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"oterolamelapau","last":"Otero Lamela","locid":"59551989-69f2-4d7d-a675-a7f07dc8a419","name":"Otero Lamela, Elena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"42451f7e-e9b1-49b8-ad46-3c450430a8d2","name":"Nilsson, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-6251-9842","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tim","key":"tolkernielsenpau","last":"Tolker-Nielsen","locid":"3cdd7c13-7576-4d34-8c3c-6b1bae91acc0","name":"Tolker-Nielsen, Tim","orcid":"0000-0002-9751-474X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29164822"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mbo3.552","issn":["20458827"],"issue":"2","journal":"MicrobiologyOpen","paperid":"e00552","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"MicrobiologyOpen","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034786508"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5493a809-0722-4a07-b777-2239920f476a","ku-85055aac-7bcd-45d4-98b1-db7628d5d2ed"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A transposon mutant library of<i> Bacillus cereus</i> ATCC 10987 reveals novel genes required for biofilm formation and implicates motility as an important factor for pellicle-biofilm formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.33-018825","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Extracellular DNA (eDNA) has been shown to be important for biofilm stability of the endodontic pathogen Enterococcus faecalis. In this study, we hypothesized that treatment with DNase prevents adhesion and disperses young E. faecalis biofilms in 96-well plates and root canals of extracted teeth. Methods: E. faecalis eDNA in 96-well plates was visualized with TOTO-1®. The effect of DNase treatment was assessed in 96-well plates and in extracted single-rooted premolars (n=37) using a two-phase crossover design. E. faecalis was treated with DNase (50 Kunitz/mL) or heat-inactivated DNase for 1 h during adhesion or after 24 h of biofilm formation. In 96-well plates, adhering cells were quantified using confocal microscopy and digital image analysis. In root canals, the number of adhering cells was determined in dentine samples based on colony forming unit counts. Data from the 96-well plate were analyzed using one-tailed t-tests, and data from extracted teeth were analyzed using mixed-effect Poisson regressions. Results: eDNA was present in wells colonized by E. faecalis after 1 h of adhesion and 24 h of biofilm formation; it was removed by DNase treatment, as evidenced by TOTO®-1 staining. DNase treatment reduced the area covered by cells in 96-well plates after 1 h (P<0.05), but not after 24 h (P=0.96). No significant differences in the number of adhering cells were observed in extracted teeth after 1 (P=0.14) and 24 h (P=0.98). Conclusion: DNase treatment does not disperse endodontic E. faecalis biofilms. The sole use of DNase as an anti-biofilm agent in root canal treatments is not recommendable.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schlafer, Sebastian","Garcia, Javier","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Væth, Michael","Neuhaus, Klaus W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-187752"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schlafer, Sebastian"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bern"],"keyword":["Adhesion","Autolysis","Biofilm","DNase","Endodontic biofilms","Enterococcus faecalis","Ex vivo","Extracellular DNA","Release"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of dnase treatment on adhesion and early biofilm formation of enterococcus faecalis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85067239407","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-187752","identifier":[{"id":"85067239407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000442553500004","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-6648f0ab-4c0b-4a2b-b9f7-60aa9eb6f83f"],"keyword":["AUTOLYSIS","Adhesion","DNase","EX-VIVO","EXTRACELLULAR DNA","Enterococcus faecalis","RELEASE","biofilm","endodontic biofilms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D380150640E6A7F8B94EDC9833D76DE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Javier","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","locid":"0c5738c1-e65b-4e34-bba4-4bc634142853","name":"Garcia, Javier","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"vaethpau","last":"Vaeth","locid":"b646a6f8-cf55-4b01-9c73-f252a48f9fdd","name":"Væth, Michael","name_org":"Vaeth, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus W.","key":"neuhauspau","last":"Neuhaus","name":"Neuhaus, Klaus W.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14744/eej.2018.55264","issn":["25480839"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Endodontic Journal","pages":"82-86","publisher":"Kare Publishing","status":"p","title":"European Endodontic Journal","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067239407"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6648f0ab-4c0b-4a2b-b9f7-60aa9eb6f83f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of DNase treatment on adhesion and early biofilm formation of Enterococcus faecalis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-187752","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Adherence to a low-gluten diet has become increasingly common in parts of the general population. However, the effects of reducing gluten-rich food items including wheat, barley and rye cereals in healthy adults are unclear. Here, we undertook a randomised, controlled, cross-over trial involving 60 middle-aged Danish adults without known disorders with two 8-week interventions comparing a low-gluten diet (2 g gluten per day) and a high-gluten diet (18 g gluten per day), separated by a washout period of at least six weeks with habitual diet (12 g gluten per day). We find that, in comparison with a high-gluten diet, a low-gluten diet induces moderate changes in the intestinal microbiome, reduces fasting and postprandial hydrogen exhalation, and leads to improvements in self-reported bloating. These observations suggest that most of the effects of a low-gluten diet in non-coeliac adults may be driven by qualitative changes in dietary fibres.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Hansen, Lea Benedicte Skov","Roager, Henrik Munch","Søndertoft, Nadja B.","Gøbel, Rikke Juul","Kristensen, Mette Bredal","Vallès-Colomer, Mireia","Vieira-Silva, Sara","Ibrügger, Sabine","Lind, Mads Vendelbo","Mærkedahl, Rasmus Baadsgaard","Bahl, Martin Iain","Madsen, Mia Linda","Havelund, Jesper","Falony, Gwen","Tetens, Inge","Nielsen, Trine","Allin, Kristine H.","Frandsen, Henrik Lund","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Sparholt, Morten H","Holck, Jesper","Blennow, Andreas","Moll, Janne Marie","Meyer, Anne S","Hoppe, Camilla","Poulsen, Jørgen H","Carvalho, Vera","Sagnelli, Domenico","Dalgaard, Marlene Danner","Christensen, Anders Fogh","Lydolph, Magnus","Ross, Alistair B","Villas-Bôas, Silas G","Brix, Susanne","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Buschard, Karsten","Linneberg, Allan","Rumessen, Jüri Johannes","Ekstrøm, Claus Thorn","Ritz, Christian","Kristiansen, Karsten","Nielsen, H Bjørn","Vestergaard, Henrik","Færgeman, Nils J","Raes, Jeroen","Frøkiær, Hanne","Hansen, Torben","Laurit