,"name":"Raes, Jeroen","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne","key":"frøkiærhannepau","last":"Frøkiær","locid":"67cbee0f-a387-4ed0-865d-a73419550125","name":"Frøkiær, Hanne","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramneek","key":"guptaramneekpau","last":"Gupta","locid":"30724a41-c0f1-4bed-bfaa-55f981d21304","name":"Gupta, Ramneek","orcid":"0000-0001-6841-6676","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lotte","key":"lauritzenlottepau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"4263561d-003a-4d4c-9f05-06a8f88155e8","name":"Lauritzen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0001-7184-5949","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Rask","key":"lichttineraskpau","last":"Licht","locid":"b5270ea1-1dc7-4db8-8644-c7ef75331664","name":"Licht, Tine Rask","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-9574","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Oluf Borbye","key":"pedersenolufpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0a2a7ad3-1719-43c6-bdf3-c3491a43a8af","name":"Pedersen, Oluf","name_org":"Pedersen, Oluf Borbye","orcid":"0000-0002-3321-3972","rank":52,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30425247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-018-07019-x","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"4630","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056452791"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","clinical microbiomics","clinical microbiomics a/s","clinical-microbiomics a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-768564b7-f553-46bd-b641-c18491719897","ku-32f6a287-6b33-4713-9058-05a50fee0140","sdu-5267237b-720c-48b2-9173-3bf41ccd6eb3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A low-gluten diet induces changes in the intestinal microbiome of healthy Danish adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.74-035308","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Staphylococcal biofilm formation is a severe complication of medical implants, leading to high antibiotic tolerance and treatment failure. Ultra-dense poly(ethylene glycol) (udPEG) coating resists adsorption of proteins, polysaccharides and extracellular DNA. It is therefore uniquely resistant to attachment by Staphylococcus epidermidis, which remains loosely adhered to the surface. Our aim was to determine if S. epidermidis remains susceptible to antibiotics when adhering to udPEG, and if udPEG coatings can improve the treatment outcome for implant-associated infections. We tested the in vitro efficacy of vancomycin treatment on recently adhered S. epidermidis AUH4567 on udPEG, conventional PEG or titanium surfaces using live/dead staining and microscopy. udPEG was then applied to titanium implants and inserted subcutaneously in mice and inoculated with S. epidermidis to induce infection. Mice were given antibiotic prophylaxis or a short antibiotic treatment. One group was given immunosuppressive therapy. After five days, implants and surrounding tissue were harvested for CFU enumeration. Only few S. epidermidis cells adhered to udPEG compared to conventional PEG and uncoated titanium, and a much lower fraction of cells on udPEG survived antibiotic treatment in vitro. In vivo, the bacterial load on implants in mice receiving vancomycin treatment was significantly lower on udPEG-coated compared to uncoated implants, also in neutropenic mice. Our results suggest that the improved outcome results from the coating's anti-adhesive properties that leads to less biofilm and increased efficacy of antibiotic treatment. Thus, the combination of udPEG with antibiotics is a promising strategy to prevent acute implant-associated infections that arise due to perioperative contaminations. STATEMENT OF SIGNIFICANCE: Infections of medical implants is an ever-present danger. Here, bacteria develop biofilms that cannot be eradicated with antibiotics. By using an ultra-dense polymer-brush coating (udPEG), bacterial attachment and the subsequent biofilm formation can be reduced, resulting in increased antibiotic susceptibility of bacteria surrounding the implant. udPEG combined with antibiotics proved to significantly reduce bacteria on implants inserted into mice, in our animal model. As the coating is not antibacterial per se, it does not induce antimicrobial resistance and its effect is independent of the bacterial species. Our results are encouraging for the prospect of preventing and treating implant-associated infections that arise due to perioperative contaminations.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Skovdal, Sandra Maria","Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Petersen, Eskild","Jensen-Fangel, Søren","Ogaki, Ryosuke","Zeng, Guanghong","Johansen, Mikkel Illemann","Wang, Mikala","Rohde, Holger","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-179081"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf"],"keyword":["Bacterial biofilms","Biofilm","Biomaterials","Implant associated infection","PLL g PEG","Staphylococcus epidermidis","Titanium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultra dense polymer brush coating reduces staphylococcus epidermidis biofilms on medical implants and improves antibiotic treatment outcome","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85049440803","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-179081","identifier":[{"id":"30078425","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000442055600005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85049440803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-573b29b9-ab72-47c0-82f0-325f2f4cb390"],"keyword":["BACTERIAL BIOFILMS","BIOMATERIALS","Biofilm","Implant-associated infection","PLL-g-PEG","Staphylococcus epidermidis","Titanium"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01E98129A6E0E51696DDE186E7716C7F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university medical center hamburg eppendorf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra M","key":"skovdalpau","last":"Skovdal","locid":"8e6b7c72-2732-402b-940c-ca02967599bd","name":"Skovdal, Sandra Maria","name_org":"Skovdal, Sandra M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis Pedersen","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eskild","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"91c7ce03-d7e1-4557-91ca-bbd19ac0b7fe","name":"Petersen, Eskild","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"jensenfangelpau","last":"Jensen-Fangel","locid":"9822ac67-91e2-4c70-be62-1d560c6e4ba6","name":"Jensen-Fangel, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryosuke","key":"ogakipau","last":"Ogaki","locid":"3ee7810d-e08c-49e2-988e-20c5f9b98a85","name":"Ogaki, Ryosuke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghong","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","locid":"41d64164-8293-4f51-b1b8-96ac2ccc6db5","name":"Zeng, Guanghong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Illemann","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"521aaf8b-4d7a-4672-82c4-2c79a297b02a","name":"Johansen, Mikkel Illemann","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikala","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7f0a4d8a-4a88-4382-84c3-58e5151bb8cf","name":"Wang, Mikala","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","name":"Rohde, Holger","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke L","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30078425"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.actbio.2018.07.002","issn":["17427061","18787568"],"issn_org":["17427061"],"journal":"Acta Biomaterialia","pages":"46-55","publisher":"Acta Materialia Inc","status":"p","title":"Acta Biomaterialia","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049440803"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-573b29b9-ab72-47c0-82f0-325f2f4cb390"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ultra-dense polymer brush coating reduces Staphylococcus epidermidis biofilms on medical implants and improves antibiotic treatment outcome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-179081","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Pathogenic bacteria can spread between individuals or between food items via the surfaces they share. Limiting the survival of pathogens on surfaces, therefore, presents an opportunity to limit at least one route of how pathogens spread. In this study, we propose that a simple coating with the essential oil isoeugenol can be used to circumvent the problem of bacterial transfer via surfaces. Methods and Results: Two commonly used materials, stainless steel and polyethylene, were coated by physical adsorption, and the coatings were characterized by Raman spectroscopy, atomic force microscopy and water contact angle measurements. We quantified and visualized the colonization of coated and uncoated surfaces by three bacteria: Staphylococcus aureus, Listeria monocytogenes and Pseudomonas fluorescens. No viable cells were detected on surfaces coated with isoeugenol. Conclusions: The isoeugenol coating prepared with simple adsorption proved effective in preventing biofilm formation on stainless steel and polyethylene surfaces. The result was caused by the antibacterial effect of isoeugenol, as the coating did not diminish the adhesive properties of the surface. Significance and Impact of the Study: Our study demonstrates that a simple isoeugenol coating can prevent biofilm formation of S. aureus, L. monocytogenes and P. fluorescens on two commonly used surfaces.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Christina Krogsgård","Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","Zeng, Guanghong","Salmi, Zakaria","Kjems, Jørgen","Mygind, T.","Snabe, T.","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-266925"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"keyword":["Biofilm","Essential oil","FILMS","FRESH","Isoeugenol","Listeria monocytogenes","Mechanism","Polyethylene","Pseudomonas fluorescens","Spoilage","Stainless steel","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antibacterial isoeugenol coating on stainless steel and polyethylene surfaces prevents biofilm growth","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85038250721","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-266925","identifier":[{"id":"29119696","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000418453800016","type":"wos"},{"id":"85038250721","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f11f98f2-cdbe-4c61-9007-b4f1bec3217a"],"keyword":["FILMS","FRESH","Listeria monocytogenes","MECHANISM","Pseudomonas fluorescens","SPOILAGE","Staphylococcus aureus","biofilm","essential oil","isoeugenol","polyethylene","stainless steel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5C216A82AF3107CFB7B74DC4794231F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","