","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85038250721"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f11f98f2-cdbe-4c61-9007-b4f1bec3217a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Antibacterial isoeugenol coating on stainless steel and polyethylene surfaces prevents biofilm growth","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-266925","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The aim of this study was to analyse arsenic (As) transformation and biosorption by indigenous As-resistant bacteria both in planktonic and biofilm modes of growth. Methods and Results: As-resistant bacteria were isolated from industrial waste water and strain PT2, and identified as Exiguobacterium profundum through 16S rRNA gene sequencing was selected for further study. As transformation and biosorption by E. profundumPT2 was determined by HPLC-ICP-MS analysis. Planktonic cultures reduced 3·73 mmol l −1 As 5+ into As 3+ from artificial waste water effluent after 48-h incubation. In case of biosorption, planktonic cultures and biofilms exhibited 25·2 and 29·4 mg g −1 biomass biosorption, respectively. As biosorption kinetics followed Freundlich isotherm and pseudo second-order model. Biofilm formation peaked after 3 days of incubation, and in the presence of As stress, biofilm formation was significantly affected in contrast to control (P < 0·05). Homogeneous nature of mature biofilms with an increased demand of nutrients was revealed by minimum roughness and maximum surface to biovolume ratio measured through CLSM analysis. Conclusion: Indigenous As-resistant E. profundumPT2 was found capable of As transformation and biosorption both in the form of planktonic cultures and biofilms. Significance and Impact of the Study: Indigenous biofilm forming E. profundum PT2 revealing As biosorption and biotransformation potential is presented an eco-friendly and cost-effective source for As remediation that can be implemented for waste water treatment.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rehman, Saba","Andreasen, Rasmus","li, Y","Rehman, Y","Ahmed, M.","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Sabri, A.N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-268454"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Pakistan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Henan University","The Women University Multan","University of the Punjab"],"keyword":["Biofilms","Bioremediation","Wastewater treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prospective role of indigenous exiguobacterium profundum pt000000000002 in arsenic biotransformation and biosorption by planktonic cultures and biofilms","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85040660195","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-268454","identifier":[{"id":"85040660195","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29130635","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f3e8a5ca-b363-4965-bc00-243698cf616b"],"keyword":["arsenic biotransformation","arsenic resistance","biofilms","bioremediation","wastewater treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F2D22E6BAE6F973C0C5EF342C018D7A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, Ny Munkegade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pk","key":"university of the punjab","loc":["Pakistan","Asia, South"],"name":"University of the Punjab","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pk","key":"the women university multan","loc":["Pakistan","Asia, South"],"name":"The Women University Multan","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"henan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Henan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Saba","key":"rehmansabapau","last":"Rehman","locid":"92fa0379-57f2-486b-aba7-963b9d4a8c94","name":"Rehman, Saba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"andreasenrasmuspau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"4e5c61a6-b382-402a-986d-7e55877e8893","name":"Andreasen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-9737-1243","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Y","key":"liypau","last":"li","name":"li, Y","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y","key":"rehmanypau","last":"Rehman","name":"Rehman, Y","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"ahmedmpau","last":"Ahmed","name":"Ahmed, M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A.N.","key":"sabrianpau","last":"Sabri","name":"Sabri, A.N.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29130635"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jam.13636","issn":["13645072"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","pages":"431-443","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","volume":"124"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040660195"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f3e8a5ca-b363-4965-bc00-243698cf616b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prospective role of indigenous Exiguobacterium profundum PT2 in arsenic biotransformation and biosorption by planktonic cultures and biofilms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-268454","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Many bacteria in biofilm surround themselves by an extracellular matrix composed mainly of extracellular polysaccharide (EP), proteins such as amyloid-like fibers (ALF) and nucleic acids. While the importance of EP in attachment and acceleration of biofilm by a number of different bacterial species is well established, the contribution of ALF to attachment in multispecies biofilm remains unknown. The study presented here aimed to investigate the role of TasA, a precursor for ALF, in cell-cell interactions in dual-species biofilms of Bacillus subtilis and Streptococcus mutans. Expression of major B. subtilis matrix operons was significantly up-regulated in the presence of S. mutans during different stages of biofilm formation, suggesting that the two species interacted and modulated gene expression in each other. Wild-type B. subtilis expressing TasA adhered strongly to S. mutans biofilm, while a TasA-deficient mutant was less adhesive and consequently less abundant in the dual-species biofilm. Dextran, a biofilm polysaccharide, induced aggregation of B. subtilis and stimulated adhesion to S. mutans biofilms. This effect was only observed in the wild-type strain, suggesting that interactions between TasA and dextran-associated EP plays an important role in inter-species interactions during initial stages of multispecies biofilm development.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Duanis-Assaf, Danielle","Duanis-Assaf, Tal","Zeng, Guanghong","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Reches, Meital","Steinberg, Doron","Shemesh, Moshe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-139601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Shemesh, Moshe"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["Agricultural Research Organization of Israel","All Global Affiliations","Hadassah University Medical Centre","Hebrew University of Jerusalem"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell wall associated protein tasa provides an initial binding component to extracellular polysaccharides in dual species biofilm","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-27548-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-139601","identifier":[{"id":"29921978","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6008451","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85048886642","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-11bdd111-083a-4202-8131-15f4b224c32e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2E7EFEAD38CADF9CE1DD160FCBA088A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/143696128/s41598_018_27548_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-27548-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"agricultural research organization of israel","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Agricultural Research Organization of Israel","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"hadassah university medical centre","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Hadassah University Medical Centre","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"il","key":"hebrew university of jerusalem","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Hebrew University of Jerusalem","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Danielle","key":"duanisassafdaniellepau","last":"Duanis-Assaf","name":"Duanis-Assaf, Danielle","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tal","key":"duanisassaftalpau","last":"Duanis-Assaf","name":"Duanis-Assaf, Tal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghong","key":"zengguanghongpau","last":"Zeng","locid":"41d64164-8293-4f51-b1b8-96ac2ccc6db5","name":"Zeng, Guanghong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Meital","key":"rechesmeitalpau","last":"Reches","name":"Reches, Meital","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Doron","key":"steinbergdoronpau","last":"Steinberg","name":"Steinberg, Doron","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Moshe","key":"shemeshmoshepau","last":"Shemesh","name":"Shemesh, Moshe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29921978"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-018-27548-1","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"9350","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048886642"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-11bdd111-083a-4202-8131-15f4b224c32e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Cell wall associated protein TasA provides an initial binding component to extracellular polysaccharides in dual-species biofilm","t