Termiske kameraer i fremtidens trafikplanlægning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-106916","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Self-performed mechanical tooth cleaning does usually not result in complete biofilm removal, due to the complex oral anatomy and the strong adhesion of the biofilm to the tooth. Therefore, different supportive measures are employed, most of which aim at the chemical eradication of bacteria in dental biofilms. As their bactericidal action impacts the entire oral microflora, agents that inhibit biofilm formation without killing bacteria, such as the bovine milk protein osteopontin, have gained increasing attention. Here, we investigate the adhesion of 8 bacterial species associated with dental caries to salivary-coated flow-cells in the presence or absence of osteopontin or the control protein caseinoglycomacropeptide (0.32 mM/L). After 1h of flow (9.45 mm/min) at 35 °C, adhering bacteria were quantified by digital image analysis in a total of 692 bright-field images. Experiments were performed in technical and biological duplicates. Bifidobacterium dentium, Rothia dentocariosa and Streptococcus mutans did not adhere to the flow cell, irrespective of the presence of osteopontin. Osteopontin reduced the adhesion of Actinomyces naeslundii, Actinomyces viscosus, Lactobacillus paracasei subsp. paracasei, Streptococcus mitis and Streptococcus oralis with 74.0%, 62.4%, 90.0%, 89.6% and 81.5%, respectively, compared to protein-free saliva. All reductions were statistically significant (p<0.05) and significantly stronger than the reductions observed for caseinoglycomacropeptide (p<0.05). ), as determined by two-sample t-tests. The broad range anti-adhesive effect of osteopontin on dental bacterial strains might explain the reduced biofilm formation observed and be exploited in vivo for increased caries control.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Schlafer, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218229"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-09","place":"Athen, gr","start":"2016-07-06","title":"ORCA - 63rd Annual Congress of the European Organisation for Caries Research","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bovine milk osteopontin targeting bacterial adhesion for biofilm control","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000445087","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-218229","identifier":[{"id":"27119144","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9c0caf04-5964-411c-b3df-6f53098c2565"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-35335750650CC545F0EE72AEEA3A7E43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000445087","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology and Caries Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathilde Frost","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3db74fb4-c382-451d-bd24-abea0bc2092c","name":"Kristensen, Mathilde Frost","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27119144"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000445087","issn":["00086568","1421976X"],"issn_org":["00086568"],"journal":"Caries Research","pages":"185","paperid":"11","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Caries Research","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c0caf04-5964-411c-b3df-6f53098c2565"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bovine milk osteopontin - Targeting bacterial adhesion for biofilm control","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-218229","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Pernille Ommen","Hansen, Bente Kring","Hansen, Line","Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","Kjems, Jørgen","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-223887"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-02","place":"Seoul, kr","start":"2016-08-30","title":"International Symposium on Staphylococci and Staphylococcus infectionsI","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aptamers as possible targeting agents for delivery of antibiotics to s aureus biofilms","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-223887","ids":["au-a5e575e2-4395-4d7d-bc16-ab9bd80f0281"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AD8D0E7911B7A88EE25C00CBF5DD361E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Ommen","key":"andersenpernilleommenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"58da0d0a-5fe3-4f73-a179-046c37fc0b70","name":"Andersen, Pernille Ommen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente Kring","key":"hansenbentekringpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3f32b0a5-11b4-4137-8a23-11362648542f","name":"Hansen, Bente Kring","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"hansenlinepau","last":"Hansen","locid":"729ea402-8050-4923-a2a1-2bfeb5a6fd63","name":"Hansen, Line","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"nielsenjespersejruppau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"721272e9-869d-48f0-b183-980b58848b68","name":"Nielsen, Jesper Sejrup","name_org":"Nielsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemsjørgenpau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a5e575e2-4395-4d7d-bc16-ab9bd80f0281"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Aptamers as possible targeting agents for delivery of antibiotics to S. aureus biofilms","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-223887","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Food spoilage and foodborne illnesses are two global challenges for food manufacturers. Essential oils are natural antibacterials that could have a potential for use in food preservation. Unfortunately high concentrations are needed to obtain the desired antibacterial effect, and this limits their use in food due to their adverse organoleptic properties. Encapsulation could make essential oils more effective by concentrating them in the aqueous phase of the food matrix where the bacteria are present. Here we tested encapsulation of the essential oil isoeugenol in spray-dried emulsions as a means of making isoeugenol a more effective antibacterial for use in food preservation. We used β-lactoglobulin and n-OSA starch as emulsifiers, and some emulsions were coated with positively charged chitosan to promote the contact with bacteria through electrostatic interactions. The antibacterial efficacy was quantified as the minimal bactericidal concentration in growth media, milk and carrot juice. The emulsion encapsulation system developed in this study provided high loading capacities, and encapsulation enhanced the efficacy of isoeugenol against Gram-positive and -negative bacteria in media and carrot juice but not in milk. Chitosan-coating did not enhance the efficacy further, possibly due to the aggregation of the chitosan-coated emulsions. The encapsulation system is easy to upscale and should be applicable for encapsulation of similar essential oils. Therefore, we believe it has potential to be used for natural food preservation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Christina Krogsgård","Kjems, Jørgen","Mygind, Tina","Snabe, Torben","Schwarz, Karin","Serfert, Yvonne","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-246459"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kiel University"],"keyword":["Chitosan","Emulsion","Essential oil","Food preservation","Isoeugenol","Spray drying"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing the antibacterial efficacy of isoeugenol by emulsion encapsulation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963692257","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-246459","identifier":[{"id":"27089032","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84963692257","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ccef6b44-aa5e-47aa-b84f-9cf99fe53070"],"keyword":["Chitosan","Emulsion","Essential oil","Food preservation","Isoeugenol","Spray-drying"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FDA857BAF7CF9BD2E90A6921501A14D2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"kiel university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Kiel University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Krogsgård","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e7e6ebef-9f08-46d3-9065-2facd5e8a570","name":"Nielsen, Christina Krogsgård","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"kjemspau","last":"Kjems","locid":"f5915d75-aca3-437a-9a9d-f4fdfef7accd","name":"Kjems, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-4128-9317","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina","key":"mygindpau","last":"Mygind","name":"Mygind, Tina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"snabepau","last":"Snabe","name":"Snabe, Torben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"schwarzpau","last":"Schwarz","name":"Schwarz, Karin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"serfertpau","last":"Serfert","name":"Serfert, Yvonne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27089032"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2016.04.002","issn":["01681605","18793460"],"issn_org":["01681605"],"journal":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","pages":"7-14","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","volume":"229"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963692257"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","dupont aps (nutrition & health) - denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ccef6b44-aa5e-47aa-b84f-9cf99fe53070"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Enhancing the antibacterial efficacy of isoeugenol by emulsion encapsulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-246459","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: Caries is caused by acid production in biofilms on dental surfaces. Preventing caries therefore involves control of microorganisms and/or the acid produced. Here, calcium-phosphate-osteopontin particles are presented as a new approach to caries control. The particles are made by co-precipitation and designed to bind to bacteria in biofilms, impede biofilm build-up without killing the microflora, and release phosphate ions to buffer bacterial acid production if the pH decreases below 6. Analysis of biofilm formation and pH in a five-species biofilm model for dental caries showed that treatment with particles or pure osteopontin led to less biofilm formation compared to untreated controls or biofilms treated with osteopontin-free particles. The anti-biofilm effect can thus be ascribed to osteopontin. The particles also led to a slower acidification of the biofilm after exposure to glucose, and the pH always remained above 5.5. Hence, calcium-phosphate-osteopontin particles show potential for applications in caries control.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Schlafer, Sebastian","Birkedal, Henrik","Olsen, Jakob","Skovgaard, Jonas","Sutherland, Duncan S","Wejse, Peter Langborg","Nyvad, Bente","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-273094"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biofilms","Calcium","Dental caries","Osteopontin","Phosphorus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calcium phosphate osteopontin particles for caries control","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84961908049","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-273094","identifier":[{"id":"26923119","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84961908049","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fbfdcaaa-b8c5-434b-9200-25c03368ae8a"],"keyword":["Biofilms","calcium","dental caries","osteopontin","phosphorus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C26E49E5FF1A6595C27FD649F5C1FA3B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Oral Ecology and Caries Control","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"schlaferpau","last":"Schlafer","locid":"bcd4e1fe-3a80-4288-8b5f-d105f6f53982","name":"Schlafer, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2463-1926","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"e5418e07-b317-4ecc-a9df-8bdedaa32f5b","name":"Birkedal, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-4201-2179","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"9d339e39-e0f1-45d6-87b3-9ab81e57599a","name":"Olsen, Jakob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"0ad646ff-89ba-439f-9d34-c606ad3ab729","name":"Skovgaard, Jonas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Duncan","key":"sutherlandpau","last":"Sutherland","locid":"5c5c563f-ca05-4219-b60d-8a3d6303ff2f","name":"Sutherland, Duncan S","name_org":"Sutherland, Duncan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Langborg","key":"wejsepau","last":"Wejse","name":"Wejse, Peter Langborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bente","key":"nyvadpau","last":"Nyvad","locid":"f0fda280-eb7a-42d4-93f0-45f26e30fc45","name":"Nyvad, Bente","orcid":"0000-0002-9545-0447","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26923119"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08927014.2016.1141199","issn":["08927014","10267867"],"issn_org":["08927014"],"issue":"4","journal":"Biofouling","pages":"349-357","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Biofouling","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961908049"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fbfdcaaa-b8c5-434b-9200-25c03368ae8a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Calcium-phosphate-osteopontin particles for caries control","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-273094","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: Clove oil is an essential oil used as a biodegradable antibacterial agent in food and pharmaceutical products. Emulsions are used to stabilize and increase the antimicrobial efficacy of oils in aqueous solutions. Smaller droplets provide better distribution of the oil. In this study, we formulate clove oil in aqueous solution by nanoemulsion. The aim of this study was to optimize key parameters in the preparation of clove oil nanoemulsion to obtain stable emulsions with less than 50 nm droplet size. The evaluated parameters include the concentration of clove oil, concentration of emulsifier, hydrophilic–lipophilic balance (HLB) number, and ultrasonication time. We determined the following response parameters: droplet size, polydispersity index, and zeta potential, and we aimed to achieve <50 nm droplet size with low polydispersity index and a highly negative zeta potential. The optimization and evaluation was obtained via Taguchi method. Taguchi method identified the concentration of clove oil and the HLB as the most affecting factors in the preparation of nanoemulsions. The optimum conditions for the preparation of nanoemuslion such as mean droplet size, polydispersity index, and zeta potential were 50 nm, 0.49 and −40.7 mV, respectively. This formulation of clove oil resulted in minimum inhibitory concentration against Escherichia coli and Bacillus cereus of 16 and 32 μg/ml, respectively, and minimal bactericidal concentrations of 16 and 64 μg/ml, respectively.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Shahavi, Mohammad Hassan","Hosseini, Morteza","Jahanshahi, Mohsen","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Darzi, Ghasem Najafpour"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-157028"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Shahavi, Mohammad Hassan"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Babol Noshirvani University of Technology"],"keyword":["Antibacterial","Clove oil","Droplet size","Nanoemulsion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clove oil nanoemulsion as an effective antibacterial agent taguchi optimization method","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84945218628","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-157028","identifier":[{"id":"84945218628","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-307a0b5f-7053-43a0-9a98-453818823a6f"],"keyword":["Antibacterial","Clove oil","Droplet size","Nanoemulsion","Taguchi optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EF5E57E1E256BC707B420C13D2581B4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"babol noshirvani university of technology","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Babol Noshirvani University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Hassan","key":"shahavipau","last":"Shahavi","locid":"81fde6d0-7738-41cd-b950-f75cded3840d","name":"Shahavi, Mohammad Hassan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morteza","key":"hosseinipau","last":"Hosseini","name":"Hosseini, Morteza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"jahanshahipau","last":"Jahanshahi","name":"Jahanshahi, Mohsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ghasem Najafpour","key":"darzipau","last":"Darzi","name":"Darzi, Ghasem Najafpour","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19443994.2015.1092893","issn":["19443986","19443994"],"issn_org":["19443994"],"issue":"39","journal":"Desalination and Water Treatment","pages":"18379-18390","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Desalination and Water Treatment","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84945218628"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-307a0b5f-7053-43a0-9a98-453818823a6f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Clove oil nanoemulsion as an effective antibacterial agent : Taguchi optimization method","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-157028","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Thin polymer coatings (in tens of nanometers to a micron thick) are desired on industrial surfaces such as stainless steel. In this thickness range coatings are difficult to produce using conventional methods. In this context, surface-initiated controlled polymerization method can offer a promising tool to produce thin polymer coatings via bottom-up approach. Furthermore, the industrial surfaces are chemically heterogeneous and exhibit surface features in the form of grain boundaries and grain surfaces. Therefore, the thin coatings must be equally effective on both the grain surfaces and the grain boundary regions. This study illustrates a novel \"periodic rejuvenation of surface initiation\" process using surface-initiated ATRP technique to amplify the graft density of poly(oligoethylene glycol)methacrylate (POEGMA) brush layers on stainless steel 316L surface. The optimized conditions demonstrate a controlled, macroscopically homogeneous, and stable POEGMA brush layer covering both the grain surface and the grain boundary region. Various relevant parameters - surface cleaning methods, controllability of thickness, graft density, homogeneity and stability - were studied using techniques such as ellipsometer, X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, scanning electron microscopy-energy-dispersive X-ray, surface zeta potential, and infrared reflection-adsorption spectroscopy.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Friis, Jakob Ege","Brøns, Kaare","Salmi, Zakaria","Shimizu, Kyoko","Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","Holm, Allan Hjarbæk","Santos, Olga","Pedersen, Steen Uttrup","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Daasbjerg, Kim","Iruthayaraj, Joseph"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-234401"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Coating","Surface initiated ATRP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-GFS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-GFS","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrophilic polymer brush layers on stainless steel using multilayered atrp initiator layer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994777422","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-234401","identifier":[{"id":"84994777422","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27792314","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b81dedda-1d40-4ca3-906e-b185436e109e"],"keyword":["coating","diblock polymer brush, grain boundary","electrografting, aryldiazonium","graft density","poly(oxyethyleneglycol)methacrylate","stainless steel 316L","surface Initiated ATRP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E482B579FBAAEA0AF339FB1A2FC7819B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Applied Surface Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"grundfos","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-GFS","l3nl":"Grundfos","l3nn":"Grundfos","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Grundfos","namevar":["Grundfos A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-GFS","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Ege","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"45c9eb89-c80b-414d-90d5-169b9987e0ab","name":"Friis, Jakob Ege","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaare","key":"brønspau","last":"Brøns","locid":"9bbc3e3e-d582-4daa-8ad2-a083443a5433","name":"Brøns, Kaare","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zakaria","key":"salmipau","last":"Salmi","locid":"0e837103-e1ff-4a22-afb3-7a7e1d502e55","name":"Salmi, Zakaria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kyoko","key":"shimizupau","last":"Shimizu","name":"Shimizu, Kyoko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guruprakash","key":"subbiahdosspau","last":"Subbiahdoss","locid":"fe2008fb-b52d-4cba-9fe7-e09a24be1112","name":"Subbiahdoss, Guruprakash","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan Hjarbæk","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Allan Hjarbæk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"santospau","last":"Santos","name":"Santos, Olga","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Uttrup","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c53368bc-faff-413e-8a77-51988f2b8b5e","name":"Pedersen, Steen Uttrup","orcid":"0000-0002-8919-2576","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"daasbjergpau","last":"Daas