{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Dagnæs-Hansen, F.","Fuursted, Kurt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-194714"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correction a modified chronic infection model for testing treatment of staphylococcus aureus biofilms on implants","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0103688","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-194714","identifier":[{"id":"84924156178","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-72820350-a1aa-43db-8abe-e91759867382"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CF72EDCD008F01F6C8D83FD484675FC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0103688","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N. P.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ac385492-f707-4053-bc6e-965ba8f60360","name":"Jørgensen, Nis Pedersen","name_org":"Jørgensen, N. P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, R.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"dagnæshansenpau","last":"Dagnæs-Hansen","name":"Dagnæs-Hansen, F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"fuurstedpau","last":"Fuursted","locid":"4480caa1-e763-4685-b132-f26a60bedce8","name":"Fuursted, Kurt","name_org":"Fuursted, K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0103688","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"3","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0118124","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-72820350-a1aa-43db-8abe-e91759867382"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Correction : A Modified Chronic Infection Model for Testing Treatment of Staphylococcus aureus Biofilms on Implants","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-194714","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Proliferation of microbial population on fresh poultry meat over time elicits spoilage when reaching unacceptable levels, during which process slime production, microorganism colony formation, negative organoleptic impact and meat structure change are observed. Spoilage organisms in raw meat, especially Gram-negative bacteria can be difficult to combat due to their cell wall composition. In this study, the natural antimicrobial agents s-poly-L-lysine (epsilon-PL) and isoeugenol were tested individually and in combinations for their activities against a selection of Gram-negative strains in vitro. All combinations resulted in additive interactions between epsilon-PL and isoeugenol towards the bacteria tested. The killing efficiency of different ratios of the two antimicrobial agents was further evaluated in vitro against Pseudomonas putida. Subsequently, the most efficient ratio was applied to a raw turkey meat model system which was incubated for 96 h at spoilage temperature. Half of the samples were challenged with P. putida, and the bacterial load and microbial community composition was followed over time. CFU counts revealed that the antimicrobial blend was able to lower the amount of viable Pseudomonas spp. by one log compared to untreated samples of challenged turkey meat, while the single compounds had no effect on the population. However, the compounds had no effect on Pseudomonas spp. CFU in unchallenged meat. Next-generation sequencing offered culture-independent insight into population diversity and changes in microbial composition of the meat during spoilage and in response to antimicrobial treatment. Spoilage of unchallenged turkey meat resulted in decreasing species diversity over time, regardless of whether the samples received antimicrobial treatment. The microbiota composition of untreated unchallenged meat progressed from a Pseudomonas spp. to a Pseudomonas spp., Photobacterium spp., and Brochothrix thermosphacta dominated food matrix on the expense of low abundance species. We observed a similar shift among the dominant species in meat treated with epsilon-PL or the antimicrobial blend, but the samples differed markedly in the composition of less abundant species. In contrast, the overall species diversity was constant during incubation of turkey meat challenged with P. putida although the microbiota composition did change over time. Untreated or epsilon-PL treated samples progressed from a Pseudomonas spp. to a Pseudomonas spp. and Enterobacteriaceae dominated food matrix, while treatment with the antimicrobial blend resulted in increased relative abundance of Hafnia spp., Enterococcaceae, and Photobacterium spp. We conclude that the blend delayed the onset of spoilage of challenged meat, and that all antimicrobial treatments of unchallenged or challenged meat affect the progression of the microbial community composition. Our study confirms that the antimicrobial effects observed in vitro can be extrapolated to a food matrix such as turkey meat. However, it also underlines the consequence of species-to-species variation in susceptibility to antimicrobials, namely that the microbial community change while the CFU remains the same. Addition of antimicrobials may thus prevent the growth of some microorganisms, allowing others to proliferate in their place. (C) 2015 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hyldgaard, Morten","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Peng, Min","Hibberd, Ashley A.","Fischer, Jana","Sigmundsson, Arnar","Mygind, Tina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238105"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hyldgaard, Morten"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DuPont - US"],"keyword":["Antimicrobial activity","Beef","Diversity","Ecology","GENE","Inhibition","Isoeugenol","Liquid smoke","Listeria monocytogenes","Microbiota","Polylysine","Sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"binary combination of epsilon poly l lysine and isoeugenol affect progression of spoilage microbiota in fresh turkey meat and delay onset of spoilage in i pseudomonas putida i challenged meat","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84943274590","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-238105","identifier":[{"id":"84943274590","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26433458","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000364244700018","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-be8bebf7-e513-4fd4-852e-2b3037fd07e3"],"keyword":["ANTIMICROBIAL ACTIVITY","BEEF","DIVERSITY","ESSENTIAL OIL COMBINATIONS","Ecology","Fractional inhibitory concentration","GENE","INHIBITION","Isoeugenol","LIQUID SMOKE","LISTERIA-MONOCYTOGENES","Microbiota","PACKAGING CONDITIONS","POLYLYSINE","Sequencing","epsilon-Poly-L-lysine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81D1B32632F6FA824C0F3B9C8B3E7C93"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Dupont ApS (Nutrition & Health) - Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"dupont us","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DuPont - US","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"hyldgaardpau","last":"Hyldgaard","locid":"9ad39be6-5ea2-4bc2-83d6-1f859fbf093f","name":"Hyldgaard, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Min","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashley A.","key":"hibberdpau","last":"Hibberd","name":"Hibberd, Ashley A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jana","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Jana","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Arnar","key":"sigmundssonpau","last":"Sigmundsson","name":"Sigmundsson, Arnar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina","key":"mygindpau","last":"Mygind","name":"Mygind, Tina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26433458"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2015.09.014","issn":["01681605","18793460"],"issn_org":["01681605"],"journal":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","pages":"131-142","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","volume":"215"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84943274590"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Uni