{"abstract":"Polyethylene glycol (PEG) brushes are very effective at controlling non-specific deposition of biological material onto surfaces, which is of paramount importance to obtaining successful outcomes in biomaterials, tissue engineered scaffolds, biosensors, filtration membranes and drug delivery devices. We report on a simple 'grafting to' approach involving binary solvent mixtures that are chosen based on Hansen's solubility parameters to optimize the solubility of PEG thereby enabling control over the graft density. The PEG thiol-gold model system enabled a thorough characterization of PEG films formed, while studies on a PEG silane-silicon system examined the versatility to be applied to any substrate-head group system by choosing an appropriate solvent pair. The ability of PEG films to resist non-specific adsorption of proteins was quantitatively assessed by full serum exposure studies and the binary solvent strategy was found to produce PEG films with optimal graft density to efficiently resist protein adsorption. (C) 2015 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lokanathan, Arcot R.","Ogaki, Ryosuke","Zhang, Shuai","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Kingshott, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-173525"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kingshott, Peter"],"keyword":["Attachment","Chemisorption","Gold","LAYERS","OXIDE","Poly ethylene glycol","Polymer brushes","Polymer solubility","Protein adsorption","Self assembled monolayers","Thiol","XPS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimizing the surface density of polyethylene glycol chains by grafting from binary solvent mixtures","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84926363907","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-173525","identifier":[{"id":"84926363907","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000352214700018","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-4d9c62b7-16cf-40b2-aef8-2cf9a670a1a1"],"keyword":["ATTACHMENT","CHEMISORPTION","GOLD","LAYERS","Non-fouling","OXIDE)","POLY(ETHYLENE GLYCOL)","POLYMER BRUSHES","Poly(ethylene glycol) brushes","Polymer solubility","Protein adsorption","SELF-ASSEMBLED MONOLAYERS","THIOL","XPS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D44AB14F3A4729B5CBDD523D2D85C04"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arcot R.","key":"lokanathanpau","last":"Lokanathan","locid":"56fe202c-b628-4857-93b8-3cc3a66f554b","name":"Lokanathan, Arcot R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryosuke","key":"ogakipau","last":"Ogaki","locid":"3ee7810d-e08c-49e2-988e-20c5f9b98a85","name":"Ogaki, Ryosuke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuai","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"1b6e5a08-f4b5-44df-b8a1-a3461676093b","name":"Zhang, Shuai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kingshottpau","last":"Kingshott","locid":"05489385-9fe3-4c3e-bbd4-7ffbf51fc0b8","name":"Kingshott, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apsusc.2015.02.156","issn":["01694332","18735584"],"issn_org":["01694332"],"journal":"Applied Surface Science","pages":"134-141","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Applied Surface Science","volume":"341"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926363907"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4d9c62b7-16cf-40b2-aef8-2cf9a670a1a1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Optimizing the surface density of polyethylene glycol chains by grafting from binary solvent mixtures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-173525","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Listeria monocytogenes is able to form biofilms on various surfaces and this ability is thought to contribute to persistence in the environment and on contact surfaces in the food industry. Extracellular DNA (eDNA) is a component of the biofilm matrix of many bacterial species and was shown to play a role in biofilm establishment of L. monocytogenes. In the present study, the effect of DNasel treatment on biofilm formation of L. monocytogenes EGD-e was investigated under static and dynamic conditions in normal or diluted complex medium at different temperatures. Biofilm formation was quantified by crystal violet staining or visualized by confocal laser scanning microscopy. Biomass of surface-attached L. monocyto genes varies depending on temperature and dilution of media. Interestingly, L. monocytogenes EGD-e forms DNase-sensitive biofilms in diluted medium whereas in full strength medium DNasel treatment had no effect. In line with these observations, eDNA is present in the matrix of biofilms grown in diluted but not full strength medium and supernatants of biofilms grown in diluted medium contain chromosomal DNA. The DNase-sensitive phenotype could be clearly linked to reduced ionic strength in the environment since dilution of medium in PBS or saline abolished DNase sensitivity. Several other but not all species of the genus Listeria display DNase-sensitive and -resistant modes of biofilm formation. These results indicate that L. monocytogenes biofilms are DNase-sensitive especially at low ionic strength, which might favor bacterial lysis and release of chromosomal DNA. Since low nutrient concentrations with increased osmotic pressure are conditions frequently found in food processing environments, DNasel treatment represents an option to prevent or remove Listeria biofilms in industrial settings.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zetzmann, Marion","Okshevsky, Mira Ursula","Endres, Jasmin","Sedlag, Anne","Caccia, Nelly","Auchter, Marc","Waidmann, Mark S.","Desvaux, Mickael","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Riedel, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-193050"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","L'Institut Agro Rennes-Angers","Ulm University"],"keyword":["Bacterial biofilms","Biofilm","DNase","Expression","Extracellular DNA","Listeria monocytogenes","Osmotic pressure","Pathogen","Release","Shewanella oneidensis MR 1","Staphylococcus aureus","Virulence","agr system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dnase sensitive and resistant modes of biofilm formation in i listeria monocytogenes i","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84953851907","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-193050","identifier":[{"id":"26733972","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84953851907","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000366994800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC4686886","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6f9a89fd-358b-48a0-bb50-608b54e30a5c"],"keyword":["AGR SYSTEM","BACTERIAL BIOFILMS","DNase","EGD-E","EXPRESSION","Listeria monocytogenes","PATHOGEN","RELEASE","SHEWANELLA-ONEIDENSIS MR-1","STAPHYLOCOCCUS-AUREUS","VIRULENCE","biofilm","extracellular DNA","osmotic pressure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6BD7B30AE4E558C9EC8133DEFCC1FBD9"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ulm university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ulm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"l institut agro rennes angers","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"L'Institut Agro Rennes-Angers","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marion","key":"zetzmannpau","last":"Zetzmann","name":"Zetzmann, Marion","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mira Ursula","key":"okshevskypau","last":"Okshevsky","locid":"70b6699e-a3fc-49e2-9052-08c02dfa5bae","name":"Okshevsky, Mira Ursula","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jasmin","key":"endrespau","last":"Endres","name":"Endres, Jasmin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"sedlagpau","last":"Sedlag","name":"Sedlag, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nelly","key":"cacciapau","last":"Caccia","name":"Caccia, Nelly","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"auchterpau","last":"Auchter","name":"Auchter, Marc","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark S.","key":"waidmannpau","last":"Waidmann","name":"Waidmann, Mark S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mickael","key":"desvauxpau","last":"Desvaux","name":"Desvaux, Mickael","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"riedelpau","last":"Riedel","name":"Riedel, Christian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26733972"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2015.01428","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"1428","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84953851907"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f9a89fd-358b-48a0-bb50-608b54e30a5c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"DNase-Sensitive and -Resistant modes of Biofilm Formation in <i>Listeria monocytogenes</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-193050","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The success of Pseudomonas species as opportunistic pathogens derives in great part from their ability to form stable biofilms that offer protection against chemical and mechanical attack. The extracellular matrix of biofilms contains numerous biomolecules, and it has recently been discovered that in Pseudomonas one of the components includes β-sheet rich amyloid fibrils (functional amyloid) produced by the fap operon. However, the role of the functional amyloid within the biofilm has not yet been investigated in detail. Here we investigate how the fap-based amyloid produced by Pseudomonas affects biofilm hydrophobicity and mechanical properties. Using atomic force microscopy imaging and force spectroscopy, we show that the amyloid renders individual cells more resistant to drying and alters their interactions with hydrophobic probes. Importantly, amyloid makes Pseudomonas more hydrophobic and increases biofilm stiffness 20-fold. Deletion of any one of the individual members of in the fap operon (except the putative chaperone FapA) abolishes this ability to increase biofilm stiffness and correlates with the loss of amyloid. We conclude that amyloid makes major contributions to biofilm mechanical robustness.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zeng, Guanghong","Vad, Brian Stougaard","Dueholm, Morten Simonsen","Christiansen, Gunna","Nilsson, Martin","Tolker-Nielsen, Tim","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Otzen, Daniel"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-005895"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional bacterial amyloid increases pseudomonas biofilm hydrophobicity and stiffness","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2015.01099","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-005895","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4595789","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"WOS:000363385200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"26500638","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84946820055","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-796c243e-646c-40fc-8336-f42d3a877191","au-863fe646-5045-47cd-bc90-ac6baffba5ac","ku-f58a297c-b119-4998-9270-b9d4dd9ba439"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-03FED9F1C528A65867051FA6388F6FDC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2015.01099","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD