{"abstract":"Anaerobic oxidation of organic matter in marine sediment is traditionally considered to be coupled to oxygen reduction via a cascade of redox processes and transport of intermittent electron donors and acceptors. Electric currents have been found to shortcut this cascade and directly couple oxidation of sulphide centimeters down in marine sediment to the reduction of oxygen at the very surface1 . This electric coupling of spatially separated redox half-reactions seems to be mediated by centimeter long filamentous Desulfubulbus affiliated bacteria with morphological and ultra-structural properties suggesting that they are living electric micro cables. The mode of action of these organisms has major impacts on element cycling by redox processes, pH balances, mineral dissolution/precipitations, and electro migration of ions in marine sediment. The ability of Desulfubulbus filaments to bridge redox half-reactions in distant regions of the sediment leads to formation of electrical fields, which modifies ion transport. The local proton producing and proton consuming half reactions induces pH extremes that accelerate dissolution of iron sulphides and calcium carbonates in anoxic layers and promotes the formation of Mg-calcite and iron oxides in the oxic zone. Oxygen seems to be the major electron acceptor, and more than 40% of the oxygen consumption in sediments can be driven by long distance electron transfer from distant electron donors. The major e-donor is sulfide, which is oxidized to sulfate, and iron sulphides are the major sources for sulfide in the system. Procaryotes with the ability to perform long distance electron transmission may flourishes in marine sediments exposed to transient oxygen depletion, leaving distinct signatures of such events in the geological record.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Risgaard-Petersen, Nils","Larsen, Steffen","Pfeffer, Christian","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Schramm, Andreas","Dong, Mingdong","Song, Jie","Revil, Andre","Meister, Patric","Nielsen, Lars Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244926"],"event":{"end":"2012-08-24","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2012-08-19","title":"Isme14","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long distance electron transport in marine sediments microbial and geochemical implications","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-244926","ids":["au-ca4e78c6-3011-4b86-8bc5-54fc9ce7d2e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A2E68E000220ED0F267479EB9DB4E9E8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Geomicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for marine microbiology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"risgaardpetersenpau","last":"Risgaard-Petersen","locid":"f722845a-947c-4408-bedc-7a338f234420","name":"Risgaard-Petersen, Nils","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6841247e-dbcd-4275-b71d-1e3cba216939","name":"Larsen, Steffen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"pfefferpau","last":"Pfeffer","locid":"0a46c156-5026-4324-9020-dc9b6f9c0ee3","name":"Pfeffer, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Louise","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingdong","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"songpau","last":"Song","locid":"fc9358bf-4ff0-4160-89d4-c2c3869b8f42","name":"Song, Jie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andre","key":"revilpau","last":"Revil","name":"Revil, Andre","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Patric","key":"meisterpau","last":"Meister","name":"Meister, Patric","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b1f70e1-663b-4a12-b10c-a12dfc320c81","name":"Nielsen, Lars Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7269-4860","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ca4e78c6-3011-4b86-8bc5-54fc9ce7d2e3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long distance electron transport in marine sediments: Microbial and geochemical implications","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244926","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Propionibacteria are part of the human microbiota. Many studies have addressed the predominant colonizer of sebaceous follicles of the skin, Propionibacterium acnes, and investigated its association with the skin disorder acne vulgaris, and lately with prostate cancer. Much less is known about two other propionibacterial species frequently found on human tissue sites, Propionibacterium granulosum and Propionibacterium avidum. Here we analyzed two and three genomes of P. granulosum and P. avidum, respectively, and compared them to two genomes of P. acnes; we further highlight differences among the three cutaneous species with proteomic and microscopy approaches.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Mak, Tim N","Schmid, Monika","Brzuszkiewicz, Elzbieta","Zeng, Guanghong","Meyer, Rikke Louise","Sfanos, Karen S","Brinkmann, Volker","Meyer, Thomas F","Brüggemann, Holger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-271945"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative genomics reveals distinct host interacting traits of three major human associated propionibacteria","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2164-14-640","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-271945","identifier":[{"id":"24053623","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3848858","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84884308290","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fa0221b6-9de2-41dc-93a3-b3e88427a947"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22DD2409121DA6BD7155B31507F53444"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2164-14-640","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Bioscience, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim N","key":"maktimnpau","last":"Mak","name":"Mak, Tim N","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Monika","key":"schmidmonikapau","last":"Schmid","name":"Schmid, Monika","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elzbieta","key":"brzuszkiewiczelzbietapau","last":"Brzuszkiewicz","name":"Brzuszkiewicz, Elzbieta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanghong","key":"zengguanghongpau","last":"Zeng","locid":"41d64164-8293-4f51-b1b8-96ac2ccc6db5","name":"Zeng, Guanghong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke","key":"meyerrikkelouisepau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen S","key":"sfanoskarenspau","last":"Sfanos","name":"Sfanos, Karen S","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"brinkmannvolkerpau","last":"Brinkmann","name":"Brinkmann, Volker","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas F","key":"meyerthomasfpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Thomas F","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger","key":"brüggemannholgerpau","last":"Brüggemann","locid":"029d7735-40a7-4a8f-a552-67e496015144","name":"Brüggemann, Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-7433-0190","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24053623"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2164-14-640","issn":["14712164"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Genomics","pages":"640","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Genomics","title_org":"B M C Genomics","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84884308290"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fa0221b6-9de2-41dc-93a3-b3e88427a947"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Comparative genomics reveals distinct host-interacting traits of three major human-associated propionibacteria","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-271945","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The importance of extracellular DNA (eDNA) in biofilm formation has become increasingly clear from research on clinically relevant bacteria. This study aimed to determine whether the quantity of eDNA produced can be linked to the ability to form biofilm. We systematically quantified eDNA over time during planktonic growth and biofilm formation in Reinheimera sp. F8 and three other environmental isolates belonging to the genera Pseudomonas, Microbacterium and Serratia. eDNA in biofilms was visualised by fluorescence microscopy and quantified by PicoGreen labelling without further sample preparation, whereas eDNA in planktonic cultures was precipitated before labelling and quantification. The effect of eDNA removal was investigated by DNase treatment. eDNA appeared in the early exponential growth phase of planktonic batch cultures and the concentration peaked in the stationary phase. The concentration in biofilms differed substantially between strains and over time during biofilm development. eDNA was important for the initial attachment in all strains, and DNase treatment reduced biofilm formation in three of four strains. The extent to which eDNA accumulated in planktonic cultures or biofilms did not reflect its significance to biofilm formation, and even very low concentrations of eDNA affected biofilm formation strongly. The significance of eDNA for biofilm formation in nature may thus be more widespread than previously anticipated.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tang, Lone","Schramm, Andreas","Neu, T.R.","Revsbech, Niels Peter","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-741839"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmholtz Center for Environmental Research (UFZ)"],"keyword":["Adhesion","Biofilm","Extracellular DNA","Pseudomonas","Serratia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extracellular dna in adhesion and biofilm formation of four environmental isolates a quantitative study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1574-6941.12168","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-741839","identifier":[{"id":"84887608705","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23786537","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-5b31d8af-4359-44f7-a1c7-4de3b4ffcad2","au-9d775047-8526-44fe-8497-3631c5327028"],"keyword":["Adhesion","Biofilm","Extracellular DNA","Microbacterium","Pseudomonas","Serratia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-39F848F49129E3ED35846B234C8B87E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1574-6941.12168","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Microbiology","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - iNano-School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"helmholtz center for environmental research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Center for Environmental Research (UFZ)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","locid":"c0a4663e-ee35-44fa-a012-32a24f9ff0a3","name":"Tang, Lone","name_org":"Tang, L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas R.","key":"neupau","last":"Neu","name":"Neu, Thomas R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"N.P.","key":"revsbechpau","last":"Revsbech","locid":"cc1826f5-6d53-45c6-8db8-34976d744f28","name":"Revsbech, Niels Peter","name_org":"Revsbech, N.P.","orcid":"0000-0002-2193-262X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.L.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"f1caa4f6-bc6e-459a-a976-8843c7ea7ff3","name":"Meyer, Rikke Louise","name_org":"Meyer, R.L.","orcid":"0000-0002-6485-5134","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23786537"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1574-6941.12168","issn":["01686496","15746941"],"issn_org":["01686496"],"issue":"3","journal":"FEMS Microbiology Ecology","pages":"394-403","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"FEMS Microbiology Ecology","title_org":"F E M S Microbiology Ecology","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887608705"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5b31d8af-4359-44f7-a1c7-4de3b4ffcad2","au-9d775047-8526-44fe-8497-3631c5327028"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Extracellular DNA in adhesion and biofilm formation of four environmental isolates : A quantitative study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-741839","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
