{"abstract":"Biofilms on food processing equipment cause food spoilage and pose a hazard to consumers. The bacterial community on steel surfaces in a butcher’s shop was characterized, and bacteria representative of this community enriched from minced pork were used to study biofilm retention. Stainless steel (SS) was compared to two novel nanostructured sol-gel coatings with differing hydrophobicity. Surfaces were characterized with respect to roughness, hydrophobicity, protein adsorption, biofilm retention, and community composition of the retained bacteria. Fewer bacteria were retained on the sol-gel coated surfaces compared to the rougher SS. However, the two sol-gel coatings did not differ in either protein adsorption, biofilm retention, or microbial community composition. When polished to a roughness similar to sol-gel, the SS was colonized by the same amount of bacteria as the sol-gel, but the bacterial community contained fewer Pseudomonas cells. In conclusion, biofilm retention was affected more by surface roughness than chemical composition under the condition described in this study.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tang, Lone","Pillai, Saju","Revsbech, Niels Peter","Schramm, Andreas","Bischoff, Claus","Meyer, Rikke Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130513"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biofilm retention on surfaces with variable roughness and hydrophobicity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79952507779","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130513","identifier":[{"id":"79952507779","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-02370015-0250-482b-b4d9-0637fecb2823"],"keyword":["Gammaproteobacteria; bacterial retention; bacterial colonization; wettability; organically modified silicas (ormosil)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7BAB118D12E65A535F5C360D16AE06BB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Biological Sciences, Microbiology","Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, iNano-School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","locid":"c0a4663e-ee35-44fa-a012-32a24f9ff0a3","name":"Tang, Lone","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saju","key":"pillaipau","last":"Pillai","locid":"b1597305-17ba-42c9-9838-47658910780b","name":"Pillai, Saju","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Peter","key":"revsbechpau","last":"Revsbech","locid":"cc1826f5-6d53-45c6-8db8-34976d744f28","name":"Revsbech, Niels Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-2193-262X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"schrammpau","last":"Schramm","locid":"25080de3-b60e-46b4-a606-d99f1ec089e5","name":"Schramm, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-7614-9616","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus",